{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter","id":1395242,"title":"Garou Control over Kinfolk - a discussion (warning: triggering subject matter)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-08T22:18:42-07:00","id":1395242,"title":"Garou Control over Kinfolk - a discussion (warning: triggering subject matter)","content":"How much control do Garou exercise over their kinfolk in your chronicles?<br /> <br /> It's not something I see much discussed. Obviously, there are differences between tribes, and the extent of control over some kinfolk (like immediate family) is different from others (you know there is a settlement of kinfolk of your tribe several hours away that belongs to your tribe, but you don't know them well and out of sight is out of mind). But I think certain general rules can be determined and any exceptions noted.<br /> <br /> And by control, I mean just that - Garou telling kinfolk what to do. Who to marry, whether to mate with a Garou - even if it means being unfaithful to a spouse; how many resources to make available to the Garou, pack, sept, or the cause; career decisions because the Garou need a kinfolk at certain places of employment or skills; or any other major decision or action the Garou may want. And of course, the Garou want their kinfolk to be very loyal - so I suspect there is a lot of influence provided in terms of &quot;educating&quot; kinfolk, particularly children, in the appropriate Garou values, loyalty, and secrecy just like a cult does. And cults exercise a LOT of control over their members. And the Litany applies to Kinfolk too, so besides the human law authorities, kinfolk could be brought up to trial by Garou for something they've done.<br /> <br /> The Kinfolk background itself implies a level of control over that number of Kinfolk. And while at low levels this can be used to describe family and friends, once it is 20 or 50 kinfolk that's a very different scenario. And while a common scenario is that a Garou controls the kinfolk that &quot;belong&quot; to him as his family, it might also be kinfolk friends and neighbors without family relations.<br /> <br /> And what about kinfolk that isn't tied to a specific Garou? Can the local tribal or sept leader exercise such control over that &quot;protectorate&quot; in lieu of any specific Garou that does have such immediate ties? And if so, is that authority more limited than say it was a Garou who was a son or sister or nephew or cousin or grandmother? I think this is something the local Litany has to address.<br /> <br /> I think this is something often overlooked in games. PCs only look after the specific Kinfolk as indicated on their background, and they typically describe their relationship in ways that are sympathetic. And in online games that have a lot of Kinfolk PCs, those Kinfolk PCs are almost always enthusiastic collaborators to the Garou because those players are looking to Play House with a Garou mate, or be otherwise useful in game since its fun to do stuff. But those aren't typical NPCs. The typical NPC Kinfolk of a tribe does not have any immediate Garou relative, and probably wants to get on with their life with as little trouble as possible - even if they don't mind donating some cash just like people do their church or favored charity or political party. But those groups don't have the power to stop by and issue them instructions or make decisions for them.<br /> <br /> I think this is an issue that makes players uncomfortable. That's both understandable and weird. Understandable because it brings up lots of ethical issues. But also weird because vampire players don't have that issue with Ghouls and Retainers, and the Kinfolk background is basically a variation of that.<br /> <br /> So I'm prepared to hear lots of dissenting views on this.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Moderator Edit: I've added a trigger warning due to the later discussion of sexual assault and rape in the discussion before shutting it down.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-17-2020, 06:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T22:43:16-07:00","id":1395246,"title":"","content":"I definitely agree that this varies radically from tribe to tribe, sept to sept, and garou to garou.<br /> <br /> However assuming a baseline traditional stance, I imagine most garou would treat their kinfolk as valued and beloved family members... as well as feeling entitled to, or even obligated to, provide guidance and direction to them.<br /> <br /> I've largely imagined it as a case where traditional families tend to gravitate around garou of their bloodline, those related to them as closely as possible, but if need arise (as tragically becomes the case with the high garou mortality rate) distant kin can also gravitate towards certain garou and at some point if a family is desperate enough any garou of the same tribe may qualify as a patron.<br /> <br /> I imagine that this is the remnant of an old siege mentality that has lived within the Garou Nation for millennia. A mentality that began as early as the Impergium when kinfolk were kept close and secure for their own safety and to ensure the survival of the Garou community which would continue to be the case as Garou culture drove kinfolk to cleave together and further more to cleave towards their patron Garou.<br /> <br /> However tribes have not always co-existed peacefully in the Nation. As such, with inner and inter tribe conflicts over the course of millennia, many kinfolk families would rely upon their Garou members for protection. The Garou cleaved together into packs and septs and those packs and septs often led the involved kinfolk to flock together as well. This siege mentality dynamic is a large part of what drives the garou and kinfolk to maintain their close proximity to this day.<br /> <br /> The importance of religion and culture also cannot be understated. Regardless of tribe, becoming garou is seen as a blessing. Many if not most kenning kinfolk will be given rites and have auspices read to predict and make them turning more likely. That helps develop the culture of garou superiority which is then reinforced by the fact that the garou wield a monopoly of violence alongside the ability of being able to contact the spirits.<br /> <br /> This combination alone makes them prime to lead their families and that doesn't even begin to mention the sense of deference that many kinfolk would have to develop as a survival instinct to avoid triggering a garou to rage and frenzy. This alongside the garou's sacred roles and their ability to defend their kinfolk against marauding garou and fomori alike paves the way for garou supremacy.<br /> <br /> Yet garou are still part of the family. Many, if not most, truly do love their kinfolk. They are raised in a highly spiritual and communal culture. Most probably value the lives of their kinfolk over their own, somewhat extraordinary in the more individualist culture of the modern west.<br /> <br /> However this love does not mean the Garou don't lead their kinfolk, in fact it may even make them feel more obligated to do so. They've been taught since birth that to be garou is a manifestation of The Goddess' blessing and to become an avatar of warfare and spirituality. Most garou would truly believe that they have a responsibility to lead their family, because kinfolk can never truly comprehend the Rage or Gnosis that a garou feels as their birthright.<br /> <br /> So garou lead their kinfolk and they dictate to them as the head of any household might. They become patriarchs and matriarchs with the only check-and-balance being higher ranked garou of the same pack, sept, and perhaps tribe. Aside from that garou are obligated to steward the kinfolk.<br /> <br /> Kinfolk can't understand the spirits and the messages they deliver of Gaia's Will. Kinfolk can't go toe to toe with a marauding lone wolf or a Black Spiral Dancer. Kinfolk can't be expected to. It's (probably) not their fault. That's the garou's obligation. <br /> <br /> The first of the kill to the greatest in station...<br /> <br /> Now, there are definitely kinfolk who would chafe under this sort of patronizing and while it would naturally vary in extremity, it would lead many kinfolk, particularly in the modern night's, to depart the Garou Nation.<br /> <br /> To me, I've never understood how it could be that the Garou Nation was shrinking. They should be able to slowly but steadily constantly increase their numbers as more and more kinfolk are born.<br /> <br /> Yet as garou die and the modern world draws many kinfolk away, I can begin to see why some garou fear that the Nation is shrinking.<br /> <br /> It's not really because so many garou are dying in the war. It's because so many kinfolk have turned their back on the Nation.<br /> <br /> For whatever reason, they have decided to abandon the War. To abandon constant fear. Constant anxiety. Constant service. Constant threat of bloody death from friend and foe alike.<br /> <br /> The greatest threat to the Garou Nation may not be either the Weaver or the Wyrm, but the Garou themselves.<br /> <br /> Same as it ever was...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T22:58:58-07:00","id":1395248,"title":"","content":"I guess this is not addressed in Kinfolk: A breed apart? I haven't read that book yet...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T18:10:15-07:00","id":1395491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1395246#post1395246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So garou lead their kinfolk and they dictate to them as the head of any household might. They become patriarchs and matriarchs with the only check-and-balance being higher ranked garou of the same pack, sept, and perhaps tribe. Aside from that garou are obligated to steward the kinfolk.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think comparison to a family is appropriate, but I think it hides a lot of potential conflicts. And those conflicts will lead to hard choices that will be problems for many people.<br /> <br /> For example, parents often have to make hard decisions in order to keep the family going. But they can do so because children are dependent on their parents, and many have been conditioned to obey their parents in ways they wouldn't other adults. While the Garou see themselves in that same role, I think many kinfolk do not. Garou see kinfolk as weak and dependent because they don't have the powers of the Garou or their knowledge. But adult kinfolk aren't in the same situation as children to parents - they're responsible and providing for themselves. So not only will they chafe against Garou authority in ways that a child may, they'll also behave in ways that adults chafe against other adult authority figures. Many kinds of people see themselves in some paternal fashion to people - religious figures, political authorities, and civic leaders. That doesn't mean their demands are always met.<br /> <br /> For example, let's take a kinfolk whose a successful businessman. He was raised to be very pro-Garou, and because of his role in the human community he's been able to provide resources and influence to the Garou. But for whatever reason - justifiably or not - the Garou have gone to that well several times and keep asking for more. The first time, the kinfolk was more than happy to write the check. The second and third time, he did it as well, but with much less enthusiasm. Now he's being asked once again. To the Garou, this is a reasonable &quot;request&quot; - they feel they have a legitimate need for it (you can come up with a variety of reasons). To the kinfolk, this is jeopardizing the success of his business and his livelihood. It's not that either is &quot;wrong&quot;. It's ultimately who controls that decision. Who really &quot;owns&quot; things. Does the (local verison) of the Litany prohibit Garou from demanding things? Or does it say that the Garou ultimately have a veto.<br /> <br /> It is easy to say that the Garou should (or even that they do) try to &quot;balance&quot; their needs with the needs/rights of the kinfolk. But they will always see things different from that kinfolk. They could very well think they are balancing things correctly, and any kinfolk complaints are ultimately just selfish. At the end, it doesn't matter if the Garou think they are being fair or balanced at all as long as they ultimately get to make the decision. And that is a matter of legal authority in the Litany and how far the Garou are prepared to exercise it.<br /> <br /> So where does that authority end? Do kinfolk have rights? If so, what are they? Or are they, in a legal sense, always dependents?<br /> <br /> We can use a real world example to illustrate. In the beginning of motion pictures, there were child stars that earned incredible amounts of money. At one point, all that money was essentially considered the parents because the child was a minor. The result was that some famous child actors were essentially penniless when they became adults because their parents spent it all. In response, California passed a law that guaranteed a portion of the child performer's earnings be safeguarded in order to protect them from abuse (though even that was only 15% of earnings). Prior to that law, the minor had no right at all to the income they earned. And even with this protection, it's still a minority amount that is protected.<br /> <br /> So what's the status of a kinfolk's wealth in regards to the Garou? Is everything protected and anything provided is a &quot;gift&quot;? Is everything really the property of the &quot;proper&quot; Garou authority over that kinfolk? Is there a portion that is protected, but everything else is available to be used by the Garou? Or is it like a feudal tithe that the kinfolk &quot;owes&quot; the Garou in exchange for that Garou's &quot;protection&quot;?<br /> <br /> And in certain human societies, the authority of one's parents could be very great in certain cultures today and historically. A Roman family's pater familias could legally exercise autocratic control over all his descendants. He held certain duties to them, but also held the power over life and death over them. This did not mean fathers exercised all those powers given to them, but they legally could (at least until the laws eventually changed and restricted some of these powers). So we have lots of examples we can use to govern this.<br /> <br /> Another point is that we use the metaphor of a family. And some Garou actually are family or another close connection to kinfolk? But what happens if say there is an isolated community of 50 or 100 kinfolk. But there isn't a local Garou spawned by them. Can another Garou simply move in and &quot;adopt&quot; them (assuming this is done with whatever legally appropriate means so that it is accepted by other Garou)? And therefore some outsider Garou shows up and says, &quot;I'm now in charge. You that owns that gas station down there, be sure to keep my car tank filled up. You that owns the local grocery, be sure to deliver several bags of groceries to this address here.&quot; And so on. All these requests might be low cost to the kinfolk and even reasonable, but it'll still be very different to provide them to someone who just showed up as opposed to someone who grew up with them. Or is this something that falls to a sept collectively until a Garou of that kinfolk community's blood is born and can claim it?<br /> <br /> Currently, I'm working on including kinfolk more in the chronicles I run, so I'm working through these things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T18:10:49-07:00","id":1395492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1395246#post1395246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet as garou die and the modern world draws many kinfolk away, I can begin to see why some garou fear that the Nation is shrinking.<br /> <br /> It's not really because so many garou are dying in the war. It's because so many kinfolk have turned their back on the Nation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. And therefore it's critical to answer the question of how much authority do Garou have to control those kinfolk, at least in regards to how a sept or tribe views that authority so it is legal in the sense it is approved in the Litany (regardless of whether that authority is used, or theway the Garou decides to go about exercising it). Can they tell a kinfolk, &quot;No, you can't leave town.&quot; or 'You'll need to go to the local community college that is nearby as opposed to heading out of state to the university of your dreams?&quot; or &quot;I've decided you're to marry my packmate because she is ready to have kids and always liked you (or altenratively to strengthen the bonds between packmates, you'll marry my packmate's sibling so we'll always be family.)&quot;<br /> <br /> Obviously, that specific level of control can't be exercised on all kinfolk everywhere, but it could be used against a certain number of individual kinfolk that one Garou could have in their span of influence. So what can they legally do in terms of the local Litany?<br /> <br /> If we stop talking about things in general, and deal with specifics, things can get tough. And ugly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 06-09-2020, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T20:05:43-07:00","id":1395736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1395492#post1395492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we stop talking about things in general, and deal with specifics, things can get tough. And ugly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I very much agree with this in particular as well as a great deal of everything else you just said.<br /> <br /> The Garou Nation is a culture from another era, one that pre-dates the renaissance and the industrial revolution and everything that came with them. Those that seem particularly interested in these developments are often viewed with suspicion or outright anger, as the treatment of the Urrah by the High and Pure tribes show.<br /> <br /> While I definitely think that the specific case of individual garou, packs, septs, and tribes are important to take into account; with details often becoming the messy stuff of great stories, speaking generally has a limited effect, although it can still be quite informative.<br /> <br /> I definitely agree that while close family might be more likely to accept the interests of the Garou, there would still be messiness. How do parents deal with the fact that their child is now considered to be above them in every way that matters in much of Garou society? How do brothers and sisters deal with it? Garou culture even keeps cousins close, but the more degrees of separation there are, the stranger things are likely to become.<br /> <br /> I most certainly agree that adult kinfolk, particularly proud and capable individuals, would probably nurse lifelong bitterment that because of what seems to be a fluke of chance, they will forever be second class citizens. That some brash child deserves respect for turning into a monster and their decades of faith and service is seen as being worth less then one lucky little brat's ability to tear apart a few fomori.<br /> <br /> Many Garou probably do recognize this and I would say that dismissing the wisdom of capable kinfolk should indicate a loss of some wisdom renown and perhaps honor... yet even then, those penalties do nothing to resolve the fact that a garou will always be viewed as more important to society and have a vastly greater opportunity for renown.<br /> <br /> Garou culture offers great renown to Garou for serving in battle. Kinfolk gain a fraction of that renown for years of dutiful service. For this reason alone, as Garou are often arrogant and seem self-important, those kinfolk aware of the option may simply leave the Nation. Others may even rebel against it.<br /> <br /> When this happens, the garou have a choice. Do they let a member of their tribe leave? A person who could help the war effort and has the potential to sire or birth the next generation's warriors? Wouldn't it be a failure to let them leave? Yet what is the alternative? To drag them home for punishment? To make an example of them? Or just... let them go?<br /> <br /> It's up to the garou and the kinfolk and that's what stories are made of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T23:30:54-07:00","id":1395770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1395736#post1395736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When this happens, the garou have a choice. Do they let a member of their tribe leave? A person who could help the war effort and has the potential to sire or birth the next generation's warriors? Wouldn't it be a failure to let them leave? Yet what is the alternative? To drag them home for punishment? To make an example of them? Or just... let them go?<br /> <br /> It's up to the garou and the kinfolk and that's what stories are made of.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but I am trying to figure out guidelines for this. This is the kind of thing that can make PCs nervous. They look to me as an ST to provide them those guidelines as I'm the expert of my own chronicle of course. So I need to figure some things out in my head. Some PCs will avoid the issue entirely. Others want to clearly play it safe, and therefore need to know where that spot is. And even those who want to be at the edge or even just over it in terms of exploitation, still need to have an idea of where it stands. Either so they can attempt to justify they are not over the line, or be aware when they would be clearly over it.<br /> <br /> So that means I need do the heavy thinking beforehand. And getting feedback from you and others (eventually, I hope) I can gauge whether my ideas seem to be acceptable, or wildly out of line. I'd rather debate this first here than with my players if something turns out to be outrageous.<br /> <br /> For example, I have a small kinfolk community of several hundred out there that is isolated and kind of orphaned. They are there for the PCs to run into and adopt if they want. But I need to figure out what are expectations in terms of how they can &quot;adopt&quot; these kinfolk, and what they could reliably expect from them, and what they could &quot;earn&quot; from them, and what they really shouldn't do.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T00:45:38-07:00","id":1395785,"title":"","content":"This is just how it has been in some online games I've been, but if the kinfolk doesn't have family to watch over them, they are under a decided garou -guard.-<br /> <br /> When it comes to being mated, it isn't uncommon for garou the challenge either the kinfolk guardian or a rival for the right to mate with the kinfolk. Sometimes, the kin doesn't have a say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T10:20:16-07:00","id":1395860,"title":"","content":"Prefacing by saying that Werewolf is one of the lines I know less about, I have a couple of thoughts to offer on this interesting subject.<br /> <br /> I do think that discussing the relationship between Garou and Kinfolk has to focus on discussing each Tribe in particular. The culture and history of each Tribe leads them to view the Litany differently, emphasizing or ignoring different parts. This inevitably includes Kinfolk relations. I think asking your question about each Tribe in turn would be better than trying to find a baseline for all Garou, which would likely be so vague as to be useless.<br /> <br /> To use an example, Tribes like the Silver Fangs or Get of Fenris would be more likely to take a top-down Garou-first attitude I think, given their cultural focus on hierarchy and combat ability respectively. Tribes with more compassionate or &quot;progressive&quot; cultures, like the Children of Gaia or Bone Gnawers, seem more likely to treat their Kin in a more equitable fashion.<br /> <br /> In addition to this, I think an important consideration is the proximity of a given pack/Sept to the homeland of their Tribe. I think Garou that place higher emphasis on tradition and Tribe culture will likely be more hardline and literal in interpreting the Litany. And those Garou will likely want to live closer to the &quot;centre&quot; of those traditions. Conversely, Garou that are less interested in following those traditions will likely move away from the Tribe's traditional heartland, where they'll likely have more freedom to live and interpret the Litany their own way. Again, this would include views on Kinfolk relations. Again, speaking broadly and with little expertise, I think more traditional interpretation of the Litany, even among more &quot;progressive&quot; Tribes, leans towards a feudal hierarchy with, at best, extremely limited protections of Kinfolk independence or rights.<br /> <br /> P.S. Start work soon, but a quick note on Kinfolk views, versus Garou. Broadly speaking, Kinfolk raised more in Garou/Tribe culture, who understand &quot;the stakes&quot; of the Garou's struggle, are more likely to accept harsher conditions or give greater support to the cause. The more they are kept in the dark, for their own protection or not, the more likely they are to resent more extreme examples of domination from their Garou relatives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 06-11-2020, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T10:43:50-07:00","id":1395861,"title":"","content":"The Garou get away with as much as they can. Staying 'honourably mated' is what you should do, not what most young garou actually do: Wolves may be monogamous but a lot of men aren't if they can pull it off, and contrary to what W20 says, that animal magnetism power works on <i>any</i> human without the willpower to stave it off, regardless of their orientation or preferences. Garou are monsters. They are not nice people, they just think they're nice people. <br /> <br /> Even in, say, a &quot;nice&quot; tribe like the black furies, who would largely <i>never </i>force an innocent woman to do something they wouldn't (This may or may not apply to men, depending on the individual) they still heavily engage in tactics to keep their people in line, be it guilt, love bombardment, gifts/luxuries/nice assignments for good behaviour... the Kinfolk likely don't have any money to their name, it'd be difficult to leave. Of course, some kinfolk are kept off the reservation and have normal lives beyond the occasional weird relative who comes in to check up on them. A garou is free to cuck a kinfolk and the only thing you can do about it is get another garou on your side (Unlikely) or take advantage of the fact that the perpetrator has probably given some beneficial treatments to your partner and... Yeah, Skindancers are doing the right thing. <br /> <br /> With BSD, <b>(Warning: You may not want to read this)</b> Kinfolk are literally property to by and sell. both sexes have harems and breed like crazy, their offspring are raised to be sacrificed for Chimage or sold off to other spirals for services, fetishes or are exchanged for fresh less-related partners for which to have more children with. Kinfolk are brutalised if they step out of line and are encouraged to work against one another, werewolves are very good at tracking down their &quot;lost property&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T16:08:35-07:00","id":1395927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1395785#post1395785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is just how it has been in some online games I've been, but if the kinfolk doesn't have family to watch over them, they are under a decided garou -guard.-</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that is easy in online games when there is a limited number of Garou and Kinfolk PCs, and things like that can be arranged. Often for the purposes of encouraging roleplay and including new PCs into the game quickly. I would be surprised if the STs of those online games would have many Kinfolk NPCs they would do would this with. It seems to me that this is something restricted to PCs.<br /> <br /> In the actual setting, I wonder if such a thing is truly possible. Certainly not on a one to one basis. Depending on the setting assumptions, there can easily be 50, 100, 200 or more Kinfolk for every Garou. A single Garou could not keep track of that, much less combined with any other responsibilities they have.<br /> <br /> However, I could see certain Garou appointed &quot;Guardians&quot; over a defined Kinfolk population in the sense of 1) giving those kinfolk an official liasion to the sept and keeping a Garou eye out for those kinfolk, 2) distinguish &quot;ownership&quot; in regards to other Garou in order to prevent turf wars and regulate disputes between Garou to those kinfolk, and 3) encourage relationship building between unaffiliated Garou and unaffiliated Kinfolk so that both groups have someone to bond to and strengthen ties to the sept and encourage mating. Those &quot;guardians&quot; would be appointed to those groups that don't already have a Garou connected to them in terms of blood or other connection. I suspect the majority of Garou appointed to such positions would be Philodox and then Ragabash. Theurges would have too many distractions due to the spirit world. Ahrouns would have too much Rage. And Galliards are too entwined with the Garou society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T16:37:43-07:00","id":1395929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1395860#post1395860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think that discussing the relationship between Garou and Kinfolk has to focus on discussing each Tribe in particular.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is definitely true, but I do think we can identify a baseline for most tribes, and then diverge from that baseline as needed given the dynamics of any particular tribe or sept.<br /> <br /> This is how I would divide up the tribes in general categories:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Tribes that Exercise the Most Control over Kinfolk, including Despotic Tendencies</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Silver Fangs</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Shadow Lords</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Black Furies</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Tribes that Exercise Much Control over Kinfolk, but tend to avoid Despotic Tendencies</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Fianna</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Glass Walker</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Uktena</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Wendigo</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Tribes that Exercise Control over Kinfolk, but known for their Fairness and Compassion</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Children of Gaia</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Get of Fenris</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Silent Strider</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Tribes that don't Exercise Much Control over Kinfolk outside Immediate Family</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Bone Gnawer</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Stargazer</span><br /> <br /> I think the first, most despotic, category is obvious. Silver Fangs are obsessed with Pure Breed and use to being in charge. Shadow Lords are known for their intimidation and severity. Black Furies might be surprising, but I consider them to be particularly controlling of the male population of their kinfolk. And they are most in need of kinfolk to populate the Garou since their lack of male Garou to sire offspring makes them more dependent on their kinfolk, and thus more of a need to make sure they do their duty. I also see them as promoting a certain kind of propaganda of how Black Fury kinfolk women are supposed to behave or believe. We are going to see most of the abuses in these tribes.<br /> <br /> The second category is what I consider to be the baseline. They exercise control, but avoid most of the worst abuses of the first group. However, I'm likely to reconsider where some of these tribes should be. I'm fairly confidant that the Fianna here. They're among the most traditional of the Garou. Wendigo too are traditional in their other ways, and their kinfolk often live in easily controlled small population centers. Uktena are more expansive of incorporating new kinfolk into the tribe, but I also see them as strongly working to enculturate those new members. I thought long about Glass Walkers and initially put them elsewhere, but eventually decided to include them here. As living in urban environments, their kinfolk are constantly exposed to &quot;unGaian&quot; culture. In response, I think they need to exercise a lot of control over certain kinfolk. Although I also see them as more willing to let certain kinfolk slip away, and more willing to bring in new kinfolk.<br /> <br /> The third category is similar to the second category, and therefore close to their baseline. However, in this category are tribes who are much less likely to abuse the influence they have over their kinfolk. Their tribal culture, and thus interpretation of the Litany, prevents that. Children of Gaia are obvious. As are Silent Striders, who typically live in small family units that travel, and thus exercise limited control of people they always live around, as opposed to larger settlements. Get of Fenris may seem to be an outlier here, but a distinguishing feature of the tribe has been the care they have for their kinfolk. This was introduced early on, and I think was done in order to deliberately show a different side to the tribe than their reputation would normally inspire. I think the second category of Garou see themselves ideally in this category, but actually aren't.<br /> <br /> The fourth category are Garou who I feel barely bother to exercise control over kinfolk. Both Bone Gnawers and Stargazers are known for eschewing temporal power. Gnawers are too disorganized to assert control over their own tribe, much less its kinfolk. And Stargazers are too busy contemplating and meditating things to exercise much control. They just have other priorities.<br /> <br /> I didn't include Red Talons because I feel lupus kinfolk are an entirely different matter. And I agree that the Black Spiral Dancers treat their kinfolk as a disposable resource, limited to whatever their imagination, needs, or desires are.<br /> <br /> I'm still thinking of what &quot;the guidelines&quot; actually mean. But in terms of tribal divergence, this is how I see how the tribes divide in their interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 06-11-2020, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T16:56:11-07:00","id":1395934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1395861#post1395861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Garou get away with as much as they can.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is true, but with caveats. Garou can easily intimidate kinfolk, but there are limits. First, kinfolk know enough that they can be dangerous if they defect to the enemy - and the enemy can include normal human hunters who can be dangerous armed with silver and if they know details on human identities of werewolves and where they live. It doesn't mean just betrayal to the Wyrm. Kinfolk have more than one option. Second, Garou are codependent on their kinfolk. They need the relationship to work and to be consensual in general. This does not mean there are not abuses. Sometimes being run along cult lines, kinfolk under intense propaganda and isolated from other influences can willingly agree to a lot of things people in general wouldn't. And a Garou can be exploitative to a small number of individuals while still retaining loyalty of the greater population.<br /> <br /> But I think the biggest caveat is that the Garou are a people of law. I don't think Garou adherence to the Litany is perfect, but its better than vampires adhering to the Traditions. Furthermore, unlike the Traditions, the Garou have a real law code in the Litany. Even if it is crude and primitive by today's standards, it wouldn't be out of place for many humans for multiple thousands of years. A ghoul or other retainer has ZERO protection from a vampire in terms of the greater vampire community. I do think there are protections for kinfolk in the Litany, particular under the section of Respect Those Beneath You, but also other sections. A vampire who mistreats a retainer doesn't face any sanction by his fellow vampires. A Garou who mistreats kinfolk might see himself brought to justice by his fellow Garou - loss of renown, possibly even a Punishment Rite.<br /> <br /> So I do think kinfolk do have some kind of rights, or at least that Garou have some kind of guidelines in how they treat them. There is reciprocity involved since Garou have obligations as well. But like any unequal power relationship, it is easier for the more powerful - the Garou - to not fulfill their duties and expect more than what's required from the less powerful. So its easier for them to get away with abuse. But I do think there are limits to that abuse before other Garou of the sept step in and intervene. It's a matter of figuring out where that lies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T12:20:56-07:00","id":1396200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1395248#post1395248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess this is not addressed in Kinfolk: A breed apart? I haven't read that book yet...</div> </div> </div> </div>You should. There it is described saying that Black Furies, Children of Gaia and Bone Gnawers are the libarete and Shadow Lords, Silverclaws and Get of Fenris are the most controlling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T13:40:47-07:00","id":1396206,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> I would reverse the Black Furies and the Get of Fenris. I would think the Furies would be much more compassionate toward their Kinfolk than the Get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T14:33:28-07:00","id":1396215,"title":"","content":"Honestly I think that the thing with Black Furies and the Get of Fenris is that in some ways they are more liberal then the other and in some ways they're more exacting then the other.<br /> <br /> The Get of Fenris expect excellence and strength from all of their children, but they don't expect them to equal the Garou and where they fail, so long as they can provide communal support for the Fenris warriors there's a lot of leeway for them.<br /> <br /> The Black Furies mean while work alongside their kinfolk and give them many opportunities yet many of them probably would chafe under the doctrine of the Wyld and elements of conservative Fury ideology, particularly male fury kinfolk who must be born feeling like they started life on the wrong foot.<br /> <br /> Neither tribe are demons nor saints and I have a deep and abiding passion for both of them, but I can see where people are coming from that either tribe might have its own unique benefits and shortcomings to being kinfolk within.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T15:24:39-07:00","id":1396220,"title":"","content":"Kinfolk are litterally the only hope of the garou.<br /> This is probably the most heavy and mature theme in Werewolf. Garou are going to be extinguished really soon if they do not breed as much as possible.<br /> Think in a logical way: they are fighting an hopeless war and they need numbers, they are struggling between tradition and progress. They litterally must organize some kind of mating program in every sept. Which is a terrible thing. But the empirical truth is one:<br /> Garou.<br /> Must.<br /> Mate.<br /> And must do it as much as possible, or they will be fucked really, really soon.<br /> I'm absolutely not surprised to meet kinfolk raised far from society, in some kind of primitivist way of thinking, in certain ways, pure brainwashing.<br /> But this is their role in garou society. Indeed the garou love them and regard them as family members, loved ones and so on. I'm not talking about abuse. But on the same time, they must mate, and a lot. Which can sounds really bad. Some sept could be really hardcore on this topic. Others, with a larger number of kinfolk, maybe could be more '''''progressive'''', but with a world on fire and an almost lost war, I wouldn't bet on it.<br /> Some tribes would be of course more soft on them, I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 06-13-2020, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T16:12:56-07:00","id":1396233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1396200#post1396200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You should. There it is described saying that Black Furies, Children of Gaia and Bone Gnawers are the libarete and Shadow Lords, Silverclaws and Get of Fenris are the most controlling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, what does &quot;the libarete&quot; mean?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T16:16:19-07:00","id":1396235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1396200#post1396200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You should. There it is described saying that Black Furies, Children of Gaia and Bone Gnawers are the libarete and Shadow Lords, Silverclaws and Get of Fenris are the most controlling.</div> </div> </div> </div>propaganda!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1396206#post1396206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> I would reverse the Black Furies and the Get of Fenris. I would think the Furies would be much more compassionate toward their Kinfolk than the Get.</div> </div> </div> </div>No I'd say he has the right if it. <br /> <br /> The Get will instill certain values into their kinfolk, certainly, but they've got this 'don't like it? not worthy!' attitude to them. They'll be upset when a family member walks away, but they've fully embraced this idea that they are the warrior elite and not everyone is cut out for that.<br /> <br /> the black furries, on the otherhand, absolutely need to instill their values on others. The Get just want to destroy enemies, the Black furries want to change minds. A Get looks at someone who rejects their values as weak, a Bf looks at someone who rejects their values as an ideological subversive. A kinfolk who goes against the black furie mantra isnt just someone that isnt needed on the team, it's a person that is wrong and dangerous and would threaten the team if not corrected. A girl that wants a 'traditional' household needs to be 'saved' whilst a male kin looking for a submissive wife is a villain who has spat in the face of the tribe. A 'soft' Get kin might get derision but the tribe doesnt really want to keep soneone who doesnt want to be there around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T18:59:47-07:00","id":1396271,"title":"","content":"Both the Get of Fenris and Black Furies are militant tribes and have been shown as ruthlessly killing humans when they've felt like it. So these are not nice people. Both have also been shown as capable of compassion and mercy towards their own favored groups. I gave my reasons why I placed them in my schema, but I'm not surprised these are the ones that some people dispute. That's why I noted for both of these tribes that their location might be surprising. I think that's OK. In an early draft of the post, I placed these tribes (and several others) differently before I gave serious thought to the list and revised them. In the end, I felt as a more ideologically driven tribe, the Black Furies would have to be more controlling of their kinfolk than the Get who are more of a military elite.<br /> <br /> People will interpret them differently based on what aspects of the tribe they prioritize above other aspects. This will vary from chronicle to chronicle. Them and the Glass Walkers were the tribes I struggled with the most. I'm comfortable with this schema and I know how I'd apply it in any given situation (which is much too complex to easily summarize in a short post). But I wouldn't complain about some other ST categorizing it differently if I was playing in someone else's game. <br /> <br /> So while I can defend my placement of these tribes in that system, I would not say that people who disagree with me are &quot;wrong.&quot; If someone argued that the Bone Gnawers were extremely controlling, but the Shadow Lords were not, I'd be heavily tempted to say the person was flat out wrong. But the Get and Furies? Let differences live.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T03:53:45-07:00","id":1396343,"title":"","content":"I'd say silver fangs need a level on their own.<br /> <br /> children of gaia, and this might just be my bias towards them, probably aren't that nice. I mean, the CoG make the most use of their kinfolk out of all the tribes in combating the wyrm (GW not withstanding. GW at least keep their kinfolk in with cushy jobs that pay well whilst CoG are pushing their kin into politically active possitions for their own ends). That can be really trying, and like the BF (but to a lesser extent) the CoG are a tribe bound by ideology more than a culture (If anything, imagine CoG culture to be quite broad and encompassing and thus less clearly defined)<br /> <br /> Then there's the fianna. <br /> they're rabbits. but they're also bad people. maybe they've got little control and despotic tendancies at the same time <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> lastly, SS<br /> They arent really around their kinfolk enough to really control them. They're like your nice/weird uncle/aunt who visits sometimes. They might give you some cash, entertain your kids with mythology and go as far to suggest a marriage arrangement, but there probably isnt much more there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T07:23:40-07:00","id":1396372,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> fair enough","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T07:27:11-07:00","id":1396373,"title":"","content":"Also, and I won\u2019t go into detail because this forum is not the place for it, but there is a difference between submissive sexually (which I don\u2019t think the Black Furies would mind) and submissive to your husband in real life (which the Black Furies would definitely oppose).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T12:13:32-07:00","id":1396440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1396343#post1396343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say silver fangs need a level on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>They could be given their desire to retain high pure breed and what they do to insure it stays within the tribe. Rather than put them in a separate place though, I felt it was sufficient to put them on the top where other tribes could join them. There can be a range within each &quot;tier&quot;. I'm less concerned about differences within each tier as I am in distinguishing between tiers.<br /> <br /> That list is for my own edification, but I shared it because I think it would benefit discussion. But if people comprise their own list differently to organize their own thoughts, that's fine. I think players will come up with their own approach to this issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1396343#post1396343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">children of gaia, and this might just be my bias towards them, probably aren't that nice. I mean, the CoG make the most use of their kinfolk out of all the tribes in combating the wyrm (GW not withstanding. GW at least keep their kinfolk in with cushy jobs that pay well whilst CoG are pushing their kin into politically active possitions for their own ends). That can be really trying, and like the BF (but to a lesser extent) the CoG are a tribe bound by ideology more than a culture (If anything, imagine CoG culture to be quite broad and encompassing and thus less clearly defined)</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. I definitely imagine that there are a lot of hippie style communes the Children established for their kinfolk, and that they subject their kinfolk to a lot of propaganda. But I think this is a lot of indirect control as opposed to anything overt. To give an example, I see Black Furies as not hesitating to threaten, expel, or even kill someone whom acts in a way they view as too &quot;patriarchal.&quot; This is a tribe after all that once practiced infanticide, and still practices human sacrifice. I don't see the Children of Gaia doing that at all. I see them as being more passive-aggressive or doing psychological bullying. Perhaps even innuendo that implies threats. But that's to the extent of it. Not that they're not capable of violence or don't have the urge to do so, but I do think there is some restraint in their tribal culture because of Unicorn. That's why I put them into a lower category. They still exercise control, but it has more restrictions. I put the Get of Fenris there for the same reason. I think they're pretty relaxed about most mating, career choices, etc. But I do think they push their children into competitive sports and physical activities, have a culture that prizes martial prowess and honors the military, and is unduly harsh on the physically weak and misfits. And they do raise their kinfolk in &quot;Gaian culture.&quot; If the Children of Gaia have hippie communes, then the Get of Fenris have survivalist compounds and home school. So that tier still has the Garou exercising &quot;control&quot; in certain areas, but it's more restricted than the others. The tribes in that tier still take their control of their kinfolk seriously, but are much more targeted in what areas they concentrate on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1396343#post1396343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then there's the fianna.<br /> they're rabbits. but they're also bad people. maybe they've got little control and despotic tendancies at the same time <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I view the Fianna as the gold standard of what the Garou should be like since they're the tribe most vested in Garou culture and created much of it. Practically everything they do comes up with the stamp of &quot;approval.&quot; I think they'll represent whatever the &quot;baseline&quot; or &quot;guideline&quot; is the most of any tribe because they'll apply the Litany to its spirit and letter. They'll still have variety in that control based on different septs and circumstances, but overall they'll be exercising a firm hand while avoiding the outright abuses of the first category. That doesn't mean they don't have abuses. Of course, they do. But they'll also have members who go more the other way as well so I think it balances out overall.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T12:51:20-07:00","id":1396450,"title":"","content":"I'm still putting down my thoughts on what that &quot;control&quot; means, but I think however a tribe applies that control, to any individual Garou that control over any individual kinfolk must vary according to their relationship to that individual kinfolk. So I'm putting kinfolk into various categories that determines how much control a Garou can exercise over them. This is based on some of the conversation we've already had here.<br /> <br /> At this point, I'm not putting down what a Garou can do to a kinfolk in each category. That will come later. Right now I'm just trying to get those categories right. Here is what I think those categories are. But I'm very open to changes and additions.<ul><li>Kinfolk who are Immediate Family to a Garou</li> <li>Kinfolk who are Extended Family, Close Friends &amp; Neighbors</li> <li>Other Tribal Kinfolk within the Sept's Protectorate that a Garou has been appointed &quot;Guardian&quot; over</li> <li>Other Tribal Kinfolk within the Sept's Protectorate</li> <li>Non-Tribal Kinfolk within the Sept's Protectorate</li> <li>Kinfolk outside of ANY Sept's Protectorate</li> </ul>The basic idea is that a Garou can exercise the most control over Kinfolk they are &quot;closer&quot; to. So the more distant the group is, the less authority one has. For those kinfolk that don't have a Garou immediately &quot;over&quot; them, then the sept in general exercises control. Sometimes they appoint guardians over them. But if guardians can't be found, then the sept still has some authority over any kinfolk in their protectorate. Lastly are those kinfolk who for any reason have fallen outside any sept's claim. These kinfolk are the most &quot;free&quot;. Some might even be unknowing kinfolk. Still, they may still have some obligations to the Garou (in the Garou's mind at least). And there has to be some sort of law or dispute mechanism that handles attempts by Garou to try to &quot;claim&quot; them. Garou society doesn't want a situation where multiple rival Garou try to control these kinfolk and end up killing each other over them.<br /> <br /> These categories are exclusive. So if you belong to one one group, you don't belong to another. Kinfolk don't need to worry about more than one Garou telling them what to do. But that doesn't mean other Garou can't put social pressure on that Garou to get them to do something she normally wouldn't do.<br /> <br /> Related are two issues I think need to be handled separately as they may not fit into the general categories above.<br /> <br /> The first is how Garou claim mates especially in the sense of whether their mate might not want to be claimed; and how disputes between Garou to that mate may be handled; and whether any rival kinfolk for that mate matters. It is highly likely that a Garou will seek a mate outside of the kinfolk they &quot;control&quot;. A Garou won't seek a mate within their immediate family. They'll be looking for someone else who is likely under the &quot;control&quot; of another Garou, and as a result that mate will change groups. So there will always be potential conflict there. Mating may not mean an exclusive relationship like a marriage. I could see in some tribes kinfolk being married to each other, but that a Garou still has sexual rights with one of them so there is a nice ready built family for any cubs.<br /> <br /> The second is some actual hardcore rights under the Litany that kinfolk should have. This can be very basic and very limited. It might only be stuff like &quot;can't be killed by a Garou without trial&quot;, or that a kinfolk's &quot;activities with the Flock that don't interfere with the Garou's protectorate aren't under Garou law&quot;. Or that a kinfolk is guaranteed to keep enough resources so that they can continue to survive. These rights should be things that are relevant to kinfolk as they were back in the Stone Age because the Litany would have been created back then and reflect that. So it may be of limited use now, but some things are eternal.<br /> <br /> So do you think the categories should be changed? I think once we have a general sense of good categories, we can distinguish what can happen in each one.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd of course, feel free to comment on any earlier posts. We're not moving on from those discussions. Just adding another item to the agenda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T14:32:51-07:00","id":1396496,"title":"","content":"Alrighty so looking over The Litany, I think that these are probably the tenets of it that are the most relevant for a discussion regarding kinfolk:<br /> <br /> \u2022Respect the Territory of Another<br /> \u2022Submission to those of Higher Station<br /> \u2022The First Share of the Kill for the Greatest in Station<br /> \u2022Respect Those Beneathe Ye - All Are of Gaia<br /> <br /> I would also argue that to a certain degree the tenets 'Accept An Honorable Surrender', 'Ye Shall Not Eat the Flesh of Humans', 'Do Not Suffer the People to Tend thy Sickness', 'The Leader May Not Be Challenged During Wartime', and 'Ye Shall Take No Action That Causes A Caern to Be Violated'<br /> <br /> So basically, an argument can be made that nearly every tenet of The Litany impacts the relationship between the garou and their kinfolk.<br /> <br /> I think that the categories you propose make a lot of sense and I'd say that they are most likely supported by the Garou Litany and I'll try to answer some of the questions you asked using the Litany as a guiding principle.<br /> <br /> Firstly 'You Shall Respect The Territory of Another'. I can very much see this as representing the claim that garou have over kinfolk seen as theirs. You respect another garou's claim over their family. You respect their relationship with close friends - unless it violates your territorial claim over your kinfolk. Further more these claims can arguably be expanded to your pack's territory, your sept's territory, and your tribe's territory. The question then becomes which of these territories deserves the most respect...<br /> <br /> Then there is 'Submission to Those of Higher Station'. I think we can all imagine who the garou believe to be of higher station in the relationship between garou and kinfolk. From there, the question becomes I think, how else does this apply. I would imagine it provides some answers to the prior tenets question: whose claim to territory is greater - the one who is greater in station. They are after all the best able to protect their territory. However, I can also see this becoming a matter of great tension. All things being equal, you should heed the greatest in station. Yet what happens if the Silver Fang lord demands the Right of the First Night from a fianna's kinfolk. Whose claim is greater? The Silver Fang whose station is higher or the Fianna whose claim to territory is more direct. Ask your local Philodox!<br /> <br /> The next tenet works hand and hand with the last one I feel. 'The First Share of the Kill to the Greatest in Station'. Invoked literally this already gives garou and high rank garou in particular a great deal of power, which they feel is deserved given they have the most power to offer their people's efforts. Speaking figuratively though, we see how garou can invoke this in nearly every facet of their kinfolk's life. Your monthly pay check? All yours - after your uncle takes his cut. You farm land? Tend it how you like - just make sure that your aunt never goes hungry. Your car? Sorry about what happened, but your cousin needed it. I'm sure those claw marks can be buffed out. He's garou ya know.<br /> <br /> Then we have the tenet that is meant to check all of these imbalances. 'Respect Those Beneathe Ye - All Are of Gaia'. In a perfect world, this keeps things stable. Garou ensure that their kinfolk do not want. They protect them from the Wyrm and outsiders alike. They insure the congeniality of the spirits. They work diligently to assure their kin's happiness. They fulfill their Noble Obligation.<br /> <br /> As any Bone Gnawers can tell you, this is not always the case.<br /> <br /> It's from the violation of this tenet, this most important tenet, that I imagine the vast majority of kinfolk defections can be attributed to. Everything else can chafe and be unpleasant, but if there is justice it could be bearable. If the kinfolk had what they needed, most could endure. When they are left to the cold, when they are treated like they are expendable, when they are ignored; that is when the kinfolk most often break.<br /> <br /> They leave and all the Nation is lesser for it.<br /> <br /> Each of the tenets can be argued to have implications of their own. Kinfolk should accept their position with grace - an honorable surrender. Garou should not exploit their kinfolk unnecessarily - eating their flesh. Kinfolk should always provide something to benefit The Nation - and not suffer it to tend them in their sickness or futility. They should not unjustly challenge the garou - for are the garou not leaders of kin?<br /> <br /> What I think is probably one of the greatest hammers in a garou's arsenal against the kin is the last tenet. Ye Shall Take No Action That Causes A Caern To Be Violated.<br /> <br /> The Garou Nation is an army and the kinfolk are the logistics and support branches. An army marches on its stomach and without the kinfolk, the garou cannot fulfill their duty. If the garou cannot fulfill their duty, caerns are threatened. If caerns are threatened, Gaia is imperiled. If Gaia is in peril, The Apocalypse draws near.<br /> <br /> &quot;So attend your duties kinfolk.<br /> <br /> Your failure draws further The Apocalypse...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T17:08:30-07:00","id":1396540,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11637_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11637\" data-vbnamecard=\"11637\">Gryffon15</a> they seriously still do that? Right of the First Night?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T17:13:02-07:00","id":1396544,"title":"","content":"Legally speaking, unless someone can stop them, any garou is perfectly within their rights to demand it.<br /> <br /> Whether or not it's actually practices depends on circumstances.<br /> <br /> I can't think of any canonical circumstances of it occurring... but I do recall the Ahroun chapter of the Book of Auspices mentioning that there was a long stretch of history where it was understood that garou, often ahrouns, would kidnap kinfolk during raids against other septs and tribes. These 'pairings' were often enough to earn a moniker. <br /> <br /> &quot;Ahroun Weddings&quot;<br /> <br /> So... I think the Garou Nation is entirely capable of it, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T17:20:48-07:00","id":1396549,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11637_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11637\" data-vbnamecard=\"11637\">Gryffon15</a> gross. But thanks. I didn\u2019t know that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T17:23:37-07:00","id":1396551,"title":"","content":"Yeah the Garou Nation is extremely interesting but it 100% reflects some of the grossest qualities of human history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T00:57:55-07:00","id":1396622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1396544#post1396544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Legally speaking, unless someone can stop them, any garou is perfectly within their rights to demand it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually one of the issues I wanted to address in this thread, so thanks for bringing it up.<br /> <br /> However, I haven't read anything that actually says the Garou have anything like the right of prima nocta/first night (which does not seem to have actually existed, but makes for good fiction). If there is explicit mention, please let me know.<br /> <br /> I do think Garou are able to claim mating with kinfolk even if that kinfolk doesn't want to. Arranged marriages are a very real thing, both in history and in some cultures even today. So that the Garou could do this fits right in.<br /> <br /> However, I don't think this means any Garou can claim any kinfolk. For example, I don't think the Silver Fangs could actually attempt to mate with some other tribe's kinfolk. That would likely produce a war unless that tribe agreed to do so. The nature of Silver Fang &quot;kingship&quot; is an interesting topic in itself. But to make it short, I don't think it's anything like a divine rights of king. It's more like a first among equals with certain sacral king responsibilities. Of course, the Silver Fangs absolutely would like it to be a divine right absolute monarchy. But it's just not.<br /> <br /> I'm fine with Garou raiding other sept's for mates, not because it would be legal, but because that is exactly what people of rival city-states/petty kingdoms would do in the heroic legendry of ancient cultures. Of course, those are precisely the kind of things that cause septs go to war. See the Trojan War or Deirdre of the Sorrows. So I do think it is regulated in practice in order to precisely avoid war. Many cultures have an &quot;abducting the bride&quot; tradition, but if you look closely at it, generally it is a kind of playacting with willing participants.<br /> <br /> So I think this is a complex issue, and I'm not sure where I want to fall. I do think Garou claim unwilling mates. But I think there is a select group that a Garou can safely claim those within it - something that has sept approval. But if you go outside that group, you either risk breaking the law or risking war with another sept. Defining what that group is where Garou can claim mates is at the heart of the matter.<br /> <br /> But because I am so uncertain, I want to hear dissenting views because there is a very good chance I'll change my mind.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T01:34:09-07:00","id":1396626,"title":"","content":"While there's nothing specifically about the &quot;prima nocta&quot; fantasy crap, the books DO make it very clear that Garou would regularly &quot;claim&quot; kinfolk from one another. They were counted as possessions and resources that could be won in battle, like caerns or fetishes. The Silver Fangs are specifically mentioned as having regularly claimed the best kinfolk from other tribes as their own stock. The Get of Fenris and Fianna and Fangs all took the remainder of the White Howler kinfolk that they wanted. In the Americas, the Three Brothers would often abduct kinfolk from one other, or claim them through caern conquest or the like... and later in history, other tribes would do the same to them (even the Silent Striders and Black Furies got in on the kinfolk grab-action that time around.) But then the Uktena went out and did the same thing to the Bunyip and, very probably since, kinfolk of other Fera aroudn the world...<br /> <br /> While these days it's unlikely that the Garou simply demand or conquer kinfolk from each other... they still try to poach. The Black Furies and Children of Gaia often &quot;adopt&quot; from other tribes, while Glass Walkers &quot;recruit&quot; useful kinfolk. The Bone Gnawers would take in whatever kinfolk families they find in their neighborhoods. So will the Fianna. Get of Fenris and probably Shadow Lords are probably pretty aggressive about &quot;let's you and me fight over who gets your sister&quot; (the Silver Fangs are of course, &quot;I get my own sister!) And the Uktena are still out there infiltrating kinfolk that aren't only not their tribe, but probably not even Garou kin... <br /> <br /> But yeah, all of this could easily lead to battles between packs, war between septs or even tribes. <br /> <br /> In the modern day I imagine that there is at least the pretense of consent. Of course how valid that consent is is... kind of questionable. Most Kenning kinfolk are certainly groomed to some extent by the Garou. And are you, the flimsy meat-and-balsa wood kinfolk, going to really tell your tribe's elder that you have zero interest in his idea of you being an &quot;honored mate&quot; to some other elder from the next sept over for diplomatic reasons? This dude who, last week, you saw tip off a cliath'e ear for questioning him? The cliath's ear grew back; yours won't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T10:54:43-07:00","id":1396694,"title":"","content":"I tend to have a darker view of the relationship that Garou have with kinfolk than some others. Then again, I think that the Garou can really be quite villainous if you dwell on certain aspects of their society and morality.<br /> <br /> Rape of kinfolk is likely a nearly universal practice among the Garou. Garou need to reproduce and male Garou with female kinfolk is the best way for that to happen, so if the kinfolk don\u2019t want to die or see their families torn apart before their eyes, they had best submit to what ever the Garou want. Is this always going to be the case? No, but it will very often have been. When it isn\u2019t, it\u2019s because the local Garou leaders decided to be kinder towards their kinfolk. So I imagine that a Tribe like the Children of Gaia has some taboos among the Garou about being too harsh with kinfolk. For crueler or more ruthless Garou, they take what they want and pray to Gaia that they don\u2019t want to kill you. Likely, this has been such a dominant part of kinfolk culture for so long that it\u2019s not even opposed or questioned. Kinfolk girls grow up knowing that they\u2019ll be in the local werewolf warrior\u2019s harem and that is as much an inevitability of life as growing old. <br /> <br /> This has likely been the reality of kinfolk life for thousands of years. I imagine that things may have gotten better in the last century as it\u2019s gotten harder for groups of kinfolk to remain isolated from a larger society that values rights, freedoms, and so on. Kinfolk who have been exposed to such dangerous ideas as \u201chuman rights\u201d may well need to be straightened out by their Garou masters, which may lead to resentment which wasn\u2019t in place before. There are likely a lot of kinfolk who manage to escape who would not have been able to do so in the past before there was rapid travel. <br /> <br /> While I don\u2019t see the Black Furies as being particularly kind or compassionate toward their kinfolk, in practice their kinfolk may be better off than many others because systematic rape is likely the most common persecution that kinfolk are subjected to and for Black Furies, this is likely to be a much rarer occurrence and less oppressively done, if for no other reason than the fact that it\u2019s less practical for the BF than for other tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T14:13:56-07:00","id":1396725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1396622#post1396622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> However, I haven't read anything that actually says the Garou have anything like the right of prima nocta/first night (which does not seem to have actually existed, but makes for good fiction). If there is explicit mention, please let me know.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There may be slight different sites during translation but on the german version of Changing Breeds there is a whole block on page 17 about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T14:22:00-07:00","id":1396729,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1129_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1129\" data-vbnamecard=\"1129\">Sergeant Brother</a> the Black Furies hate rape!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T15:06:28-07:00","id":1396738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1396626#post1396626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Silver Fangs are specifically mentioned as having regularly claimed the best kinfolk from other tribes as their own stock.</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">I wonder if the statements about Silver Fangs claiming the best kinfolk of other tribes still holds up for an entirely different reason than this discussion.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">If there is a general Pure Breed out there, then I can see SFs doing this. But if Pure Breed is specific to each tribe, than this wouldn't actually help the Silver Fangs. These kinfolk could only lessen their own stock of Pure Breed. They should only want to use kinfolk that can help retain their Pure Breed - those already of their own tribe.<br /> <br /> That might have been true in earlier areas when the concern about disappearing Pure Breed wasn't an issue, and the SFs could bring in &quot;new blood&quot;.</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T17:21:53-07:00","id":1396760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1396729#post1396729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1129_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1129\" data-vbnamecard=\"1129\">Sergeant Brother</a> the Black Furies hate rape!</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but if a Black Fury Ahroun decides that a particular kinfolk man would make a good father for her child, what happens to him if he says no? Will there be repercussions for him? Maybe, maybe not, but might he be wise to say yes? Probably so.<br /> <br /> Of course, that event will likely happen a lot less than with other Tribes, but I suspect that the BF probably doesn\u2019t think about that the same way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T17:54:29-07:00","id":1396765,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:13px\">As I have said before, I do think Garou can claim Kinfolk as mates though the kinfolk be unwilling (to varying degrees though we need to remember kinfolk are not defenseless and can cause trouble). But this does not mean a Garou can just claim anyone.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">A Garou's \u201cclaim\u201d of a kinfolk is also a claim made <i>against</i> another Garou. This is not terra incognita where anyone can plant a flag. It is either an individual Garou like a family member or appointed guardian, or at the general level of the sept itself (likely adjudicated by a hearing of the Sept Elders or their designate like a trusted Philodox). If those Garou don't approve of the match, or have concerns, that claim is going to be disputed. In other words, kinfolk should always have another Garou, in some capacity, to watch out over their interests. (I am not saying those interests are always protected, or not considered or overruled when convenient \u2013 but there is something there).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">That could lead to a Challenge, and the Challenger doesn't get to decide the nature of that contest.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">So I think for the most part, Garou claim mates only when they can pacify or have the approval of that kinfolk's \u201cguardian\u201d. The kinfolk might still be unwilling, but that would be no different than examples of arranged marriages among humans. We may view that as wrong, but it is not unique to the Garou. There are exceptions. </span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If they don't have approval, but the kinfolk <i>wants</i> to be the mate of the other Garou, they might be able to get away with it in some tribes/septs, though not in others. There would be some kind of precedent or example that could be followed.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If the Garou doesn't get approval and claims an unwilling kinfolk anyway, it might be accepted in certain circumstances, or it might result in punishment even leading to ostracism or worse.</span></li> </ul>Then there is the issue of kinfolk as \u201cwar booty\u201d claimed during a raid between septs. Let's be clear here \u2013 this is war pure and simple. Whether or not such a \u201cclaim\u201d is recognized depends on the outcome of the war. If your sept is defeated in the war, your claim is rejected, and that enemy sept might take its revenge on you during the war or as a price to restore peace. Only if your sept wins or there is some kind of negotiated settelment, might you keep your prize.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">In these cases, unless the sept itself has decided on war, I don't think it will support some lone Garou or a pack disrupting the peace for selfish reasons. They may force that Garou to return whatever booty was stolen. Though there could be cases where the sept decides its hand is forced and must go to war regardless. You can make sure there will be some sort of retaliation though for forcing them into an unwanted war.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u201cWar booty\u201d is a very different thing than claiming kinfolk within your sept or an allied sept.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">If it happens, I think it usually happens during the course of a war, as opposed to something that instigates one. And it is probably something more likely to have occurred in the past than nowadays. I could see this happening a lot for thousands of years from the Stone Age to the Iron Age. But how realistic is it in modern day America or Europe when abduction of kinfolk might trigger police investigation? I think this scenario must happen much less than what it once did. I can imagine scenarios where this still occurs, but I think it is a much less common one than in previous eras.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">So I think outright abduction of an unwilling kinfolk as a mate is more likely to be done when the kinfolk is somehow lost or not claimed, but somehow now identified as such. (A good example would be finding a Lost Cub, and the Garou feel that Lost Cub's siblings or cousin could also be kinfolk which they confirm with Scent of True Form.) Such a kinfolk would not have a Garou defender, and the sept is more likely to approve of something that \u201creturns\u201d a kinfolk back to the Garou. Of course, this is also the scenario that might blow up in the Garous' faces since such a kinfolk is the least \u201cconditioned\u201d to accept this and most likely to cause trouble.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Sorry for rambling, but this is how I think things through so I can figure out how I want to handle it in my own chronicles.</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T21:26:36-07:00","id":1396806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1396694#post1396694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to have a darker view of the relationship that Garou have with kinfolk than some others. Then again, I think that the Garou can really be quite villainous if you dwell on certain aspects of their society and morality.<br /> <br /> Rape of kinfolk is likely a nearly universal practice among the Garou. (...).</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright so. I'm just gonna put my neck out on this and say that, even though this is probably how such a society would probably function &quot;for real,&quot; it's <i>not</i> a real society. We do need some boundaries and barriers; at the end of the day it's a game people play for fun, and the PCs are supposed to be the heroes. If I come to your table and you tell me this about kinfolk, well I'm not even going to sit down, i'm taking the snacks I brought and heading home. I dunno, maybe someone enjoys this ultra-harsh, crapsack grimdark stuff, buuuuut. We gotta make allowances for the enjoyability of hte game, and the notions that, at the end of the day, savage as they are, Garou ARE still the heroes the universe has (even if not the heroes the universe necessarily wants or deserves.) Wanton rape of kinfolk is absolutely a gross violation of the Litany, and the act of rape itself is always described as falling solidly in the territory of the Wyrm. Are there Garou who do it? I'm sure there are. Those Garou are what you'd call &quot;the antagonists,&quot; and i'd still be careful about bringing them into the game.<br /> <br /> Heck my stuff about the dubious nature of kinfolk &quot;consent&quot; is kinda squick in my head, and falls towards what I would consider more of an extreme exception. Most Garou, once you cut away the PTSD and such, are normal humans, normal wolves, in terms of views and behavior. They are not out there to mathematically optimize cub production - especially if that would hurt the people they love, or at least diminish the feeling of 'being righteous&quot; that the Garou often define themselves by.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1396738#post1396738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I wonder if the statements about Silver Fangs claiming the best kinfolk of other tribes still holds up for an entirely different reason than this discussion.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">If there is a general Pure Breed out there, then I can see SFs doing this. But if Pure Breed is specific to each tribe, than this wouldn't actually help the Silver Fangs. These kinfolk could only lessen their own stock of Pure Breed. They should only want to use kinfolk that can help retain their Pure Breed - those already of their own tribe.<br /> <br /> That might have been true in earlier areas when the concern about disappearing Pure Breed wasn't an issue, and the SFs could bring in &quot;new blood&quot;.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I personally figure that if the Silver Fangs are grabbing kinfolk (or non-kin!) that they think are the ideal of &quot;Silver Fang Kinfolk&quot; and they just happen to be from another tribe, then it's simply like that tribe's heroic lineage culminates in the bloodline &quot;being admitted&quot; into the most heroic tribe of all. Because hey, when you think about it, the Fangs couldn't have possibly been up to their nostrils in Pure Breed when the tribe began, every bloodline in the tribe had to come from SOMEWHERE. All those Houses scattered across Eurasia, had to start somewhere. <br /> <br /> I've personally never been a fan of the Tribal Eugenics Program version of Pure breed we find in 2nd / Revised, though. the Background has caused so many go-nowhere arguments in my experience that I just hand-wave it as a mystical gibberdy-doo and move on with my day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T21:44:26-07:00","id":1396812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1396806#post1396806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alright so. I'm just gonna put my neck out on this and say that, even though this is probably how such a society would probably function &quot;for real,&quot; it's <i>not</i> a real society. We do need some boundaries and barriers; at the end of the day it's a game people play for fun, and the PCs are supposed to be the heroes. If I come to your table and you tell me this about kinfolk, well I'm not even going to sit down, i'm taking the snacks I brought and heading home. I dunno, maybe someone enjoys this ultra-harsh, crapsack grimdark stuff, buuuuut. We gotta make allowances for the enjoyability of hte game, and the notions that, at the end of the day, savage as they are, Garou ARE still the heroes the universe has (even if not the heroes the universe necessarily wants or deserves.) Wanton rape of kinfolk is absolutely a gross violation of the Litany, and the act of rape itself is always described as falling solidly in the territory of the Wyrm. Are there Garou who do it? I'm sure there are. Those Garou are what you'd call &quot;the antagonists,&quot; and i'd still be careful about bringing them into the game.<br /> <br /> Heck my stuff about the dubious nature of kinfolk &quot;consent&quot; is kinda squick in my head, and falls towards what I would consider more of an extreme exception. Most Garou, once you cut away the PTSD and such, are normal humans, normal wolves, in terms of views and behavior. They are not out there to mathematically optimize cub production - especially if that would hurt the people they love, or at least diminish the feeling of 'being righteous&quot; that the Garou often define themselves by.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't ever recall playing a game of W:tA where rape was discussed as something player characters or their allies did. I also wouldn't introduce it as part of a game. Then again, if I were playing a game set in the middle ages, there are plenty of squicky things that would surely be going on all around the characters that I wouldn't necessarily bring up in a game. I don't know that I would say that the Garou are necessarily the heroes. There was an intersection section in the first Player's Guide, called &quot;Something Wicked&quot; about emphasizing how evil Garou are as a way to express the inherent horror of the setting. Garo are, after all, the creatures who for years culled humanity, who drove other shifters to the brink of extinction, and many would want to reduce the human population dramatically. I don't think that rape would be that out of place considering the rest of Garou culture. Of course, first and foremost is having fun and anything that made players feel uncomfortable would be out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T21:45:15-07:00","id":1396813,"title":"","content":"Yeah, this is definitely one of those areas where I feel that the dials of 'Realism' and 'Narrative' are important to keep in mind.<br /> <br /> If the World of Darkness is being used to create passive narrative experiences such as books, comics, shows, movies, etc. then the creator is fully empowered to maintain their vision of setting realism or to propose some sort of alternate vision and create freely. So long as the audience is given information going in about what sort of content is being produced, they can choose whether or not they're interested in absorbing the story.<br /> <br /> When you're actually playing however, any concept of 'Realism' is far less important then 'Player Enjoyment/Interest'. Even if a game is disturbing and horrific, as long as everyone is enjoying themselves and interested (and no one gets hurt), then they're doing it right. Every group will have its own needs and every person will have their own needs. As someone with experience playing with an ST who prioritized their vision of 'Setting Realism' over player enjoyment, I can state that it gets old fast and it makes things worse for everyone involved.<br /> <br /> That's why I'm a huge advocate of things like Session 0, the X Card, and the Golden Rule. Screw what the books say, do what your group wants to do to enjoy themselves while playing a game and creating a narrative experience that is safe for everyone.<br /> <br /> Most folks probably already know this and agree with that but y'know, sometimes it warrants saying on the off chance someone out there needs to read it.<br /> <br /> (Also as to the former example, I can't say anything about creating fiction using WoD stuff but it's copyrighted so probably ain't good for anything but fan fiction sites. I'm not a lawyer. Don't use anything I say as legal advice. I'm not a mod, don't take my word here as meaning anything concrete aside from my opinion. Anyway, long disclaimer over.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T22:13:58-07:00","id":1396818,"title":"","content":"The people I role play with are all people I have known for 10 or more, sometimes 20 or more, years. We've had so much chance to get to know each other and what we're comfortable with, that it is never an issue I always have to try to remember, when on forums especially, that some gaming groups consist of people who don't know each other that well and end up butting heads, making each other uncomfortable, or otherwise having issues that my group wouldn't. In any case, in a game, the number one thing is that everybody have fun and feel comfortable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T22:33:30-07:00","id":1396820,"title":"","content":"I haven't seen any comments good or bad on my &quot;categories&quot; that distinguish different zones of control, so I'm moving forward. (Though people are still free to comment, disagree, or add anything they want).<br /> <br /> I'll start with the easiest - the kinfolk are immediate family. Maybe immediate only means the nuclear family. Maybe it is extended in the sense its immediate generations - grandparents, cousins, and such. Maybe it includes immediate neighbors. Still fairly compact. It might include in-laws if their mate's family is not already &quot;controlled&quot;. If so, Garou just gets the mate, not the in-laws. Let me know where you think the boundary should lie.<br /> <br /> So this is what I see:<br /> <br /> Garou can control people's mates - arrange marriages and the like. Typically this will either be something like &quot;marry my packmate&quot; or &quot;if you marry this other Garou or kinfolk, it is a good political alliance for me within the sept/tribe.&quot; Something that reflects the Garou as being &quot;head of the family&quot;. It might also include vetos if the Garou disapproves of the marriage for some reason. Since these are likely close blood relations, this won't include that Garou's ability to mate with them (except for perhaps Silver Fangs which can sometimes be verys squicky).<br /> <br /> Garou can call upon extensive financial obligations IF the Kinfolk are capable of it. I think it's limited to kinfolk being able to live and survive in a routine manner. A Kinfolk only available through the Kinfolk background can only give so much. But if you have a wealthier Kinfolk who owns his own business, has a high net worth, investment income, etc. then a PC who wants to use it better have it recorded as Allies or Resources. But in terms of general handling, not mechanics, I think the Garou should be able to &quot;draw the water from the well&quot; though NOT cause the well to dry except in exceptional circumstances. Even if it is limited to just the &quot;wealthy&quot; kinfolk, and how much is rich will have different opinions, I think the Garou can be very tyrannical here. I'm thinking something like 10% take &quot;for the cause&quot; on a regular basis.<br /> <br /> I also think things like directing careers, education, etc. because these are the kinds of things we see parents influence or dictate to their children.<br /> <br /> And of course normal Kinfolk Background stuff - sending people off to do errands and such, acting as the Garou's hands among the Flock because the Garou has the Curse to deal with, or can't be everywhere.<br /> <br /> So the model here is &quot;strict parent in a traditional society&quot;. Again, this is just the base guideline - tribes and septs will modify this.<br /> <br /> I think the greatest control can be exercised here because the assumption is &quot;control&quot; is always balanced by the close personal connections the Garou has with those people. Garou wants the best thing for their parents, siblings, children, cousins, best friends, neighbors, etc. So that should <i>prevent</i> the worst abuses.<br /> <br /> Of course, I still think there is some kind of supervision here. Bad treatment will reach the sept leaders who will intervene if needed, even if it is only loss of renown.<br /> <br /> I also think we need to think of rights that kinfolk have since that will be something that can override control at this level.<br /> <br /> So what are people's thoughts? Does it need to be more strict, less strict? Do we need additional examples of control because we want examples of things that may crop up in game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T22:52:48-07:00","id":1396823,"title":"","content":"I do like the categories you brought forth and I definitely agree that much of what you put here would be considered 'Best Practices' for the Garou.<br /> <br /> These are the sorts of things that I see being considered as 'the conduct of a reasonable garou'. You don't take more then you need and you don't tap the well dry, you respectfully consider your kinfolk's wishes while also considering what's in their best interest, you do what is best for the family and the tribe and Gaia as a whole. I would even say that, as the renown chart suggests, a garou conducting themselves this way should be considered for honor and/or wisdom renown.<br /> <br /> Specifics will very from tribe to tribe and sept to sept, naturally. The Fenrir might obligate all able bodied kinfolk to at least be somewhat proficient in a form of combat or a skill useful for facilitating effective combat. The Shadow Lords might be beholden to the dictates of the highest ranked Shadow Lord locally, even if it contradicts the feelings of a more closely related shadow lord. The Bone Gnawers might say 'fuck this' entirely and declare that &quot;Do As Thou Wilt&quot; shall be the whole of the law.<br /> <br /> Yet largely I think these are very solid guidelines to keep in mind as what is considered the functional assumption of Garou society.<br /> <br /> Of course stories come from disturbance to the status quo and conflict, so how often things have the luxury of being simple depends on the whims of your ST...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T07:38:50-07:00","id":1396862,"title":"","content":"My canon: <br /> <br /> Before tribes, Changing breeds were people with power, and like anyone with power, they abused it. Their egos were inflated massively by their god-given power, They took scores of the best looking mates and killed who they pleased. When they got into conflict with others, they started forming pacts with spirits for advantages In return for favours which often upset the natural order; A rabbit doesn't want to be hunted by foxes, so the rabbit spirit would ask for some fox-genoicde. The spirits eventually unionized so things wouldn't get so petty, and tribes were formed out of which spirit union the werewolves were to follow. Later, those spirit unions agreed to send the garou against the wrym spirits they don't like. <br /> <br /> Garou culture is nice enough so that they can get an ego boost out of being 'the good guys' who fight righteous battles. Then, when they abuse kinfolk, they can blame stress and the strain of fighting against an apocalyptic war. Either &quot;It's a one off&quot; or &quot;They should be doing everything they can to support their saviours&quot; depending on the offence. They need the Narrative of being the good guys, so they won't do anything obviously bad, but they are also looking to gain the most they possibly can, and their inflated egos and the narrative of the righteous warriors allows them to justify indulgences. I'm not saying every Garou is a grinning rapist who cares not for his family; they're not that cynical. They've genuinely tricked themselves into thinking they're righteous even when at times they aren't. <br /> <br /> It also helps that garou are naturally scary as fuck and are brimming with palpable rage. Even though kinfolk don't really feel that Rage, they do see rage. Maybe, Alan the Fianna is a perfectly nice young Galiard who doesn't mean any harm, but when he starts flirting with Betty the kinfolk, Betty's scared things could go bad, so she does her best to placate Alan without stiring up Rage. A man who can eviscerate you in a breath is a boy you treat seriously. So Betty cuts of contact with other men for the forseeable future (Poor Charlie) and if she can't deftly turn his attention away without upsetting him, opens her legs for Alan because that's what Alan wants. Alan's thinking &quot;Wow this is so easy I'm incredible&quot; (He probably is above average) and then, perhaps, wants to try his luck with a different woman (We'll call her Danielle) and Danielle is taken the same way as Betty. <br /> That's the shitter. Because Betty is going to feel worthless because of Danielle, but also she's going to be worried that if she goes back to Charlie, she'll upset Alan and spiral him into a rage, as that has doubtlessly happened spectacularly . Maybe Alan wouldn't care about Betty going back to Charlie, maybe he really would. She can't really confront anyone. She doesn't want to escalate anything. Maybe there are bad options there, and she'll kick herself for not taking them. When she feels she can go back to Charlie, she'll feel guilt. If Alan comes back to her, she'll feel guilt. Alan thinks he's worth a lot, Betty, Charlie and Danielle think they're worth very little. So comes the slide of increasingly dysfunctional relationships that reinforce this belief further. Maybe this is why garou prize kinfolk so much, they like people who just say yes. And when A kinfolk shows reasonable backbone, she'd be considered far more radical, because Garou just expect submisive kinfolk and aren't used to backtalk. Imagine, say, we add leon the Fianna to our example (It's been alphabetical so far, but this is a bit futher down the line) and he wants to spend time with the now-older Betty. She says no. <br /> <br /> &quot;What?&quot; Leon says. &quot;What did I do wrong?&quot; after all, Betty has been with Alan and Fred and Harry and Jack and even Kylie and she's still with the poor cuck charlie. How is Leon worse than Alan and Fred and Harry and Jack? Leon has had some pretty good &quot;ego boosts&quot; too, so this is unprecedented. The Nerve of this kinfolk! Outrageous! <br /> If he doesn't frenzy, Leon goes on to victimise Betty or Charlie <br /> <br /> It just seems to me that, sociologically, Garou society is bent on being barely sustainable. An ethnic group where maybe 1 in 30 people get phenomenal, terrifying &quot;chosen one&quot; power some time in puberty that raises their status above the other 29 is going to be a bad one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T08:04:18-07:00","id":1396872,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m sorry. Ewwwwwwww.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s too much realism in my gaming world for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T08:07:02-07:00","id":1396874,"title":"","content":"And I don\u2019t think that\u2019s the way reality works either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T09:07:15-07:00","id":1396886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1396872#post1396872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s too much realism in my gaming world for me.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1396874#post1396874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I don\u2019t think that\u2019s the way reality works either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which one is it?<br /> <br /> The Garou nation is a coalition of cults. A lot of communes deep in the wilderness following a strange doctrine with the belief that the outside world is an enemy. Real world cults are weird and you can't imagine the level of brainwashing they do to you unless you're in one, Imagine a cult with actual magical shapeshifting warriors. Sure, there's factors I didn't mention (What if Betty has a mother who's a garou?) but then there are factors concerning that (Betty's mother is probably complicit in the status quo, as it has benefited herself also. She cannot reprimand Alan without drawing attention to her own misdeeds. Also if Betty didn't want to be taken advantage of by Garou like a kinfolk she should've been born a Garou so it's really their collective faults that betty isn't.... Yeah, there's a lot of rabbit holes)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T11:11:48-07:00","id":1396902,"title":"","content":"I thought I was going to be one of those with the most negative depiction of Garou, but compared to some of the posters here I'm extremely mild!<br /> <br /> There is a power imbalance between Garou and Kinfolk, but I think it is important to remember that 1) Kinfolk have numbers, 2) Kinfolk know a lot about the Garou, and 3) Kinfolk aren't helpless. It's relatively easy for Kinfolk to get access to high purity silver. If living among the Garou really was that bad, it wouldn't be hard for a kinfolk community to pull a Sicilian Vespers and wipe out an entire sept, or sell them out to the enemy.<br /> <br /> In fact, I wouldn't be surprised if that's been done on occasion in Garou history at the most abusive septs. And while I'm sure the Garou took revenge on those specific kinfolk, I'm also sure it's lead to reforms and more protections of kinfolk in local Litanies as a result. Because no one wants to be murdered in their sleep, or see other Garou die to no benefit to Gaia or the Nation. Self-defeating eventually gets expunged.<br /> <br /> I do think terrible abuses occur, but that happens in humanity too. They are more the exceptions, and the Garou themselves identify them as abuses. Sometimes the abusive Garou get away with it. Sometimes they don't. This can be fun to explore in game for PCs. Attitudes and actions help distinguish NPCs from one another. And it allows PCs to take sides, forge alliances, and identify opponents or enemies.<br /> <br /> I think there should be conflict among Garou (as opposed to just external enemies) because it makes for a better game. And I like making kinfolk a prominent element of the setting. I feel too often I, as an ST, neglect this element in my chronicles as a real part of the setting. And I feel other STs and even Players do as well. So a discussion like this generates ideas for everyone on the type of things that could happen at a sept.<br /> <br /> I do think many Kinfolk are raised in a cultlike atmosphere. But I think this is less like Jonestown and more like a Mennonite colony (not to pick on the Mennonites, I just need a more normal example of a community that divorces itself from the larger culture). There's propaganda, conformity, isolation, and strictness, but actual crimes committed against their members are rare. This doesn't mean that there can't be some kinfolk settlements that are like Jonestown. Some septs go bad. That can be an interesting part of the setting. But I don't think it is the standard.<br /> <br /> Part of my goal here is to identify &quot;what is abuse&quot; and &quot;what is acceptable&quot;. So I can help guide the PCs of my own chronicles. What is acceptable to a Garou can be different from what is acceptable in a human community. But it should still allow a generic player of the game to play and not leave in disgust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T11:38:37-07:00","id":1396905,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> thank you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T12:48:14-07:00","id":1396922,"title":"","content":"I don't think that the kinfolk could effectively mount much of a resistance against the Garou. Especially since they will be raised to believe that their abuse is normal, not only normal but righteous, because their masters are blessed by Gaia to save reality. People raised for generations to believe such things would have a hard enough time resisting humans, much less the demigods that Garou are. <br /> <br /> I do, however, think that there is a factor that would heavily moderate what I described above, and that would be the protectors that Black Fox described. Not just protectors, but family protectors. Any group of kinfolk is going to be tied to a group of Garou, who would be their protectors or if you want to be a bit darker about it, their owners. Their lords perhaps. These Garou won't just protect those kinfolk, they will be their literal family, even immediate family. Because of the way that Garou heredity works, a Garou's parents, their children, their brothers and sisters - those are all likely to be kinfolk and those will be the kinfolk who who under that Garou's protection.<br /> <br /> So if some Garou wants to go and rape a kinfolk, in all likelihood he was be raping his pack mate's sister, mother, or daughter. That Garou would likely be raping his own cousin. That isn't going to go over too well and would cause a lot of fight's and bad blood. A Garou from another pack or sept or Garou group who does so would be unofficially declaring war by raping the immediate family members of another group of Garou. <br /> <br /> So I think that overt rape would be rare, because of the above reasons. Though there would still likely be a lot of pressure on kinfolk to consent to a Garou's advances and how much pressure does there have to be before the consent isn't really consent anymore? I imagine that every few Garou see themselves as rapists and very few kinfolk see themselves as being raped. The holy one wants sex, you should feel lucky to be chosen, how perverse would be be to say no? Likely this situation would be handled in a more orderly manner, like arranged marriages, than just Garou getting an urge and selecting a kinfolk. <br /> <br /> I imagine that there would be a similar mindset for other Garou requests. If a kinfolk owns a business and a local leading Garou asks for money, or for them to sell the business, or otherwise do something that hurts financially - the kinfolk would be expected to comply even if there were no obvious fear of retribution. It is as though a devout Christian were just visited by a literal angel, displaying miracles, who asked for money - few would dream of saying no. <br /> <br /> I think that in all of these cases, that there would be an issue of chain of command. A pack leader or influential elder may be able to make extravagant demands upon kinfolk and that would be seen as entirely justified. Other Garou, though, would likely face negative repercussions if they abused their authority over kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T14:40:12-07:00","id":1396946,"title":"","content":"So, I don't make all of my septs super grimdark. <br /> If things get bad enough, you'll start spawning banes and there will be traitors. On the otherhand, Garou do get to spin the &quot;Enemies of the sept are so much worse Oh My God let me tell you about the tale of these spirals and a pentex executive we hunted down&quot;. A strong external enemy is very good at disuading internal enemies. <br /> <br /> However, I think there's a kind of chronic abuse there where you don't even realise it's abuse, you just think it's normal. And say, the story with Betty, that's a very slow burning drama of a young woman, not something you'd go to court over. <br /> <br /> There are kinfolk very close to very nice garou<br /> <br /> and there are kinfolk that are much closer to some not very nice garou<br /> <br /> There are very abusive Stargazers and there are peak-kindness Shadow Lords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T18:55:29-07:00","id":1396984,"title":"","content":"Okay. I thought about this. Any Garou who treats their Kinfolk that way is gonna fall to the Wyrm very quickly. Rape is probably literally the worst crime anyone can commit. Gaia, the Mother Goddess, would not tolerate her children being treated that way by Garou who claim to worship Her. A Garou may be opposed (even violently opposed) to letting one of their Kinfolk get involved with someone unsuitable. But they would NOT rape her. They just wouldn\u2019t.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T19:02:23-07:00","id":1396986,"title":"","content":"Yeah, rape is one of those things which is going to undoubtedly be feeding banes, if not creating banes, like absolutely no one's business.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T20:45:27-07:00","id":1397004,"title":"","content":"Kinfolk fill the same role in Werewolf that Retainers (especially ghouls, but not limited to them) do in Vampire. They both provide servants for the main supernatural character that can act in the mundane world on behalf of their master. But vampire retainers have it far worse than kinfolk. However, that darkness can easily be elided during vampire chronicles. One reason for that, I think, is that while many things vampires do to retainers are abusive, most of them are metaphors for actual real world violations. Feeding on people, turning them into vampires or ghouls, using mental and emotional disciplines like Presence and Dominate, are obvious metaphors of rape and other abuse. But because they are metaphors and not the act itself, it can be easier to digest.<br /> <br /> I wonder if there is something similar that can be done to Kinfolk that could be metaphor of certain abuses that if stated directly could be too much for the gaming table. But would make a good stand in.<br /> <br /> We need to use proper &quot;source material&quot; as inspiration from actual werewolf legends, folk tales, and popular culture. It can't be something arbitrary and new, but something that would click immediately in people's head as &quot;yeah, that would happen to werewolves&quot;. Like something that shows kinfolk as being complicit in any &quot;crimes&quot; of the werewolf. Like eating any bloody meat they bring in (from animals they killed in wolf form), but never being allowed to ask where it came from (as this is a universal taboo in &quot;trained&quot; kinfolk - because it would bring &quot;bad luck&quot; but the real reason is that doing so might inadvertently harm the veil). I think expectations of <i>silence </i>from Kinfolk on various matters might be good. In game, it could be used simply as an interesting taboo that gives flavor to Kinfolk. There are lots of things Kinfolk don't talk about. And they're trained in that. There is a long list of things they simply don't talk about, they don't ask questions about, and they don't answer if other people ask them.<br /> <br /> These people don't lie to cover things up. They simply are silent. They talk around things so they don't have to mention it. The taboo is that strong.<br /> <br /> It would be a good metaphor because we know victims of abuse are often told/warned to not mention it to people (because the perpetrator wants to remain hidden). Thus in less abusive kinfolk communities, this range of topics is much less. In more abusive communities, this silence becomes more and more present.<br /> <br /> In terms of having the right feel, I think this scene from An American Werewolf in London is a good example. If we translate to WoD terms, it's a tavern in a kinfolk community,with obvious signs of werewolfery present - perhaps as chiminage to spirits, a fetish, or as a sign of some kind. But despite it being out in the open, it's just completely ignored as if it isn't there. Two outsiders come in, and then ask about it. But they don't get any answer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VJRZ4kIizXY\" data-code=\"VJRZ4kIizXY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/VJRZ4kIizXY/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 06-17-2020, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T21:21:01-07:00","id":1397007,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> I like that interpretation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T21:56:59-07:00","id":1397009,"title":"","content":"Hot Damn that would be excellent inspiration for a Fianna hide-away.<br /> <br /> To the greater point though, I agree with ya Black Fox. Keeping the tradition of everything in the WoD being analogies, kinfolk as allegories for isolated (religious) communities make a lot of sense and you have lots of room to play with that notion from the tribes. Homeless communities, salarymen, hippie communes, religious gatherings, indigenous reservations, etc.<br /> <br /> I also think that homebrew ideas for kinfolk cultural taboos are exactly the sort of addenda to things like Unsung Heroes that are valuable. Cultures of silence, taboo of outsiders; I could even see some modern tribes (like the Glass Walkers) developing almost Omert\u00e0 style hardcore denialism. <br /> <br /> &quot;There's no such thing as werewolves, vampires, ghosts; or any of that other nonsense. It's all old-wives tales.&quot;<br /> <br /> The same way the family of a mobster might steel themselves and say something along the lines of:<br /> <br /> &quot;There's no such thing as the mafia.&quot;<br /> <br /> But yeah, I think that's an interesting tack and I need to go back and re-watch an American Werewolf in London someday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T01:56:59-07:00","id":1397023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1396984#post1396984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Drops bomb.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna say some ugly shit here, be warned.<br /> <br /> The evil of rape is contextual. In some cases it's an attrocity, in others it's just bad. There are even stories where characters (I've only seen this with male victims) get raped as their Just Deserts.<br /> If there was some sort of social contract going on (IE in a conflict it's expected that Men get killed, women may get raped or killed but never both) I'd argue that the women would have a lot less to fear and it'd be a less traumatic experience than being raped in a society where such a thing is abhorent and a women has to fear being killed for her silence after the rape is done.<br /> <br /> I'd argue for garou, who regularly make bloody messes, who periodically put their comrades through excrutiating punishment rights, who have a lot of pent up rage, and who are half-primitive man, half beast (I don't know much about wolves here, but I know Male lions will kill another male, kill that male's kids, and take the dead male's women as if it were normal); I don't think a lot of garou are going to see rape, or at least how they commit rape, as any more &quot;of the Wyrm&quot; than the acts they normally commit. I think many would probably differentiate their rape (Subtle, Coercive) as something else to what they think of as &quot;Actual&quot; rape ( Violently forcing the act) and many Garou rapists don't think of themselves as such as a result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T02:09:06-07:00","id":1397026,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> I totally disagree with you, but you have the right to your opinion. But I would never game with anyone who treated rape as anything other than a disgusting and horrific act.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T02:47:45-07:00","id":1397032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1397023#post1397023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm gonna say some ugly shit here, be warned.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">And I'm going to stop you right there. You really should cultivate the idea that &quot;if it feels like a bad idea to say, maybe I shouldn't say it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Rape is a heavily administrated topic here and OPP just did a seminar on controversial topics like it, consent, and psychologically triggering topics.<br /> <br /> As such, it should never be discussed like this.<br /> <br /> I'm going to leave the topic open but please stay away from the subject of sexual assault.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T02:58:32-07:00","id":1397035,"title":"","content":"My perspective on the Garou and Kinfolk is that there's a bit more give and take other than the latter being the slaves of the former. It's an uneven hierarchical arrangement but it's not quite the pyramidal relationship that vampires have with their Retainers (who are slaves, no beating around the bush). In simple terms, Kinfolk are the families of Garou and very often are the people who have raised and taught the Garou in question before they reach maturity.<br /> <br /> I'd also argue that the vast majority of decisions regarding Kinfolk marriages, raising children, and the more &quot;culty&quot; elements of their society are probably administered by the Kinfolk themselves. It is going to be the rare werewolf who has time to sit down and rule over the Kinfolk of their tribes and their lives with the majority of things handled by trusted members of their society. The Garou, by and large, are too busy fighting the Wyrm and plotting military strategy to handle the majority of logistics that fund as well as supply their war.<br /> <br /> I'd argue that a closer depiction of how Garou and Kinfolk interact would be Dynasts and the Dragonblooded. The Dragonblooded are the elite of their society, have superpowers, and are treated as demigod. The Dynasts, however, are still the nobility of the Empire. The Kinfolk are not &quot;just&quot; the beaten down members of Garou society but they are an elite compared to &quot;regular&quot; humans who they have a religion that tells them they are superior to.<br /> <br /> Because they are.<br /> <br /> It's also important to note that Dynasts and Dragonblooded have the same Venn Diagram overlap that Garou and Kinfolk do. Not all Dynasts are Dragonblooded but almost all Dragonblooded are Dynasts (accent on almost). Most Garou have grown up in the society of Kinfolk and have their friends, family, and worldview shaped by it.<br /> <br /> THE SILVER CROWN had Albrecht disgusted by the fact his father had his mother mate with another Garou in order to hopefully produce a new heir for Jacob Morningkill that inherited the Garou gene. However, his father tears Albrecht's view of the situation apart and says that his mother wanted to do it because she was disgusted by his exile. They viewed their role as a duty and Albrecht to be forsaking his.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T04:13:42-07:00","id":1397053,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I agree. Garou are the elite, but they also have a certain sense of noblesse oblige toward their Kinfolk (especially among the Silver Fangs, Fianna and Black Furies). Both Garou and Kinfolk contribute to the struggle to defend Gaia and both hate the Wyrm with equal passion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T05:59:12-07:00","id":1397071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1397032#post1397032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">And I'm going to stop you right there. You really should cultivate the idea that &quot;if it feels like a bad idea to say, maybe I shouldn't say it.&quot;</span></div> </div> </div> </div>The World Of Darkness is built around Dark subject matter. As such, I didn't feel like it was &quot;a bad idea to say&quot;. If anything, I think we should use these games more to talk about things we don't like about society. I felt compelled to warn people because <i>some</i> people have low tollerances with the topic and want it out of sight (It's a good thing you put a warning on this thread) but that doesn't mean I'm writing something I shouldn't. If you just write &quot;Rape is the worst thing ever&quot; then there's nothing to critically think about. That might suit some people but Hows and Whys are what gets the brain working. Creating a fictional culture which should have huge problems concerning the subject and then <i>pretending nothing happens</i> or presenting it as unrealistically clear cut and dry easy problem is a bigger problem for me than than writing things as they would be (even if writing things as they would be is &quot;horrible&quot;)<br /> <br /> A good storyteller should be playing devil's advocate. They shouldn't set you up as golden heroes and making every bad guy a snivelling unjustifiable monster. They should know the systems and present it in an evocative manner, and present complex villains that players can find merit and fault in. A Ramsay Bolton for your party to slaughter now and then is fun, but it's far more interesting and narratively worthwhile to have players question their own values. I mean, werewolf is a game where you play Fascist-primitivist cults that dream of genocide and <i>are the good guys relatively speaking. </i>If all the players at the table are willing to explore everything that entails, why shouldn't you explore? Of course, if players say no, you leave it, but if they don't, it seems a bit... Silly to be so limiting if everyone consents to it.<br /> <br /> Hell. World of darkness is punk. &quot;If it feels like a bad idea to say, Maybe I should try to say it as loudly as I possibly can&quot; would be more apt (But not on a forum, i gotcha) It's a place where you can play with the USA's 1950's racial politics or Stalin's regime or the Rwandan Genocide or the Checknyan concentration camps so long as you have players who are willing to work with it. The Garou are monsters powered by their rage and they literally have an innate &quot;you absolutely need to fuck me&quot;. When they enter Thrall of the Wyrm they Eat people/FuckCorpses/paint the walls in blood. They were never meant to be something comfortable.<br /> <br /> <i>What's the point in a modern setting if you can't scathingly attack everything through the power of satire? </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T06:47:46-07:00","id":1397083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1397071#post1397071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The World Of Darkness is built around Dark subject matter. As such, I didn't feel like it was &quot;a bad idea to say&quot;. If anything, I think we should use these games more to talk about things we don't like about society. I felt compelled to warn people because <i>some</i> people have low tollerances with the topic and want it out of sight (It's a good thing you put a warning on this thread) but that doesn't mean I'm writing something I shouldn't. If you just write &quot;Rape is the worst thing ever&quot; then there's nothing to critically think about. That might suit some people but Hows and Whys are what gets the brain working. Creating a fictional culture which should have huge problems concerning the subject and then <i>pretending nothing happens</i> or presenting it as unrealistically clear cut and dry easy problem is a bigger problem for me than than writing things as they would be (even if writing things as they would be is &quot;horrible&quot;)<br /> <br /> A good storyteller should be playing devil's advocate. They shouldn't set you up as golden heroes and making every bad guy a snivelling unjustifiable monster. They should know the systems and present it in an evocative manner, and present complex villains that players can find merit and fault in. A Ramsay Bolton for your party to slaughter now and then is fun, but it's far more interesting and narratively worthwhile to have players question their own values. I mean, werewolf is a game where you play Fascist-primitivist cults that dream of genocide and <i>are the good guys relatively speaking. </i>If all the players at the table are willing to explore everything that entails, why shouldn't you explore? Of course, if players say no, you leave it, but if they don't, it seems a bit... Silly to be so limiting if everyone consents to it.<br /> <br /> Hell. World of darkness is punk. &quot;If it feels like a bad idea to say, Maybe I should try to say it as loudly as I possibly can&quot; would be more apt (But not on a forum, i gotcha) It's a place where you can play with the USA's 1950's racial politics or Stalin's regime or the Rwandan Genocide or the Checknyan concentration camps so long as you have players who are willing to work with it. The Garou are monsters powered by their rage and they literally have an innate &quot;you absolutely need to fuck me&quot;. When they enter Thrall of the Wyrm they Eat people/FuckCorpses/paint the walls in blood. They were never meant to be something comfortable.<br /> <br /> <i>What's the point in a modern setting if you can't scathingly attack everything through the power of satire? </i></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with it. Shadowrun and World of Darkness are clearly dystopian settings where it is more or less tried to paint everything darker then it is now to do critic on the actual time. And because it is not overblown to much you can totally relate to, yeah that can really happen. It is saying in Core Rulebooks and again in changeing breeds and Ghouls and Revenants that those shits like rape can totally happen and is for many a normal setting but it should be part of the GMs job to clarify beforehand with the players on how much they are okay with playing out those dark things and if the players are not confortable the should be just the lucky ones that have a master where they got spared with or like in Changeing Breeds there forced marriage is actually with their (true) love.<br /> <br /> So if someone does not want to work with a setting where such dark things are more or less common they should either not work as an auther for it, as a GM play with a round that have no problem more or less ignore what happens arround them or be part of a system where there is Friede, Freude, Eierkuchen like it is said in german where with The Dark Eye is a perfect system for all is fair and (more or less) nice. WoD whas from the start conceptualized as a dark setting so there authers should not be afraid of bringing dark matters up but to overdo it with presentation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T09:00:57-07:00","id":1397100,"title":"","content":"I do think the Garou see each other as &quot;people&quot; and their kinfolk and the Flock as something less than that. But both kinfolk and other human beings (and wolves) aren't at the level of livestock. I think they are a blend of things in terms of concept and law for the Garou - they may be treated as livestock in terms of property damage and wergild, but in other ways they are full legal persons with explicit rights. Not as much as the Garou themselves have, but they still have some (within a range of course depending on tribe and sept). I think collectively kinfolk are a mix of livestock, pets, legal inferiors, and full equals to the Garou. It just depends on what <i>context</i> you are talking about.<br /> <br /> If I had to pick one analogy for them, I think serfdom might be a good one. Serfs are dependent on their feudal lord and have additional duties and restricted rights compared to free peasants, but also had certain rights and were entitled to certain protection and justice.<br /> <br /> I also don't see kinfolk as having <i>less</i> rights than ordinary humans. And ordinary humans too are supposed to be protected. In Renown Award examples, we're given examples for both protecting and not protecting helpless humans, and for having good or poor relations with nearby Kinfolk. The Garou term for mundane humanity is the Flock which I've always taken to have double meanings. On the one hand, wolves devour the sheep in a flock. On the other hand, it implies the Garou are the shepherds of the Flock.<br /> <br /> My own model for Garou behavior and society isn't some kind of totalitarian version of Jonestown. It's the aristocratic warrior societies of Ancient Greece, the Ulster Cycle, Beowulf, and Russian Bylinas. There may be many objectionable things about Garou culture and values, but I and none of the people I have ever played with ever modeled them on the SS, NKVD, or Red Guards. If I'm looking for a flawed Garou with tragic flaws, my inspiration would be Agamemnon, not Lavrentiy Beria.<br /> <br /> I also think it is important to repeat that this thread is about figuring out the guidelines or normal standard for Garou in terms of handling their Kinfolk and the demands that can be made from them. It is OK to mention outlying behavior or things that may be acceptable at fringe septs. But let's make clear that they are not typical. And outright criminal behavior should be mentioned as things that are not allowed (even though they may still happen, because Garou have their criminals as well, and not all criminals are brought to justice).<br /> <br /> And the standards that we should be looking for are things that can used during play. Most players don't want to be the equivalent of gulag guards. They're seeking to emulate something like Lon Chaney, Jr. and Maria Ouspenskaya in the Wolf Man movies.<br /> <br /> I think this thread has a real benefit to me and to others, so guys, let's not cause it to be closed. If you really want to talk about all the awful things the Garou can do, please start your own thread so if it is shut down, it doesn't affect this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T09:19:33-07:00","id":1397103,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">It's not a matter of satire. It's a matter that sexual assault is a subject that can literally have traumatic flashback inducing effects. Hence why its something that has to be discussed very carefully.<br /> <br /> It's also not up for debate but a rule of the company.<br /> <br /> Just letting you guys know.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T10:19:39-07:00","id":1397111,"title":"","content":"I think that the majority of Garou authority over kinfolk is going to be of the soft variety, it is implied and/or cultural. You do what Garou want not because they will inflict violence on you if you don\u2019t, but because that is just what is done. The Garou are Gaia\u2019s chosen and you\u2019re blessed enough to be in the position to serve them.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that is what kinfolk might think who are raised in an insular world of kinfolk and Garou. But I wonder how many kinfolk and Garou have that kind of upbringing and how many grow up essentially in the modern secular human world. On one hand, I could see a group of kinfolk living in some kind of compound in the woods that have no electricity, no running water, no access to modern media, no cars, etc. Something like the Amish, maybe even more extreme because their culture might be even more hostile to the outside world than that of the Amish. On the other hand, I guess it\u2019s possible to have kinfolk grow up completely immersed in mainstream modern human culture, going to public school, watching TV, playing sports, going on dates, and so on. My wife and I home school Our kids and, while we\u2019re atheists, we know a number of other families who are part of the Christian fundamentalist homeschooling community and they are fairly often not familiar with aspects of culture that some people would think are universal and often they know about things or have ideas that many people are unfamiliar with. <br /> <br /> I could see kinfolk falling into anywhere on that spectrum and the degree of isolation that they have from the mainstream of society is going to be tied to how normal they view obedience to werewolves.<br /> <br /> In some ways, those kinfolk who are more connected to mainstream human society are potentially the most useful. A bunch of kinfolk living in a secret compound in the woods who are subsistence farmers and don\u2019t know what a TV set is may be more obedient, but not as useful as a kinfolk who owns a law firm. Kinfolk with money and connections would be able to offer Garou access to things that most Garou would have a lot of difficulty getting for themselves, because it\u2019s hard to be Gaia\u2019s warrior and have a day job. But if your kinfolk cousin runs a law firm, chances are he won\u2019t stand at attention quite as fast when you snap your fingers and he likely gained a lot of ideas about human rights from exposure to modern society. The law firm kinfolk would probably have to come from a more liberal Tribe that would accept their kin having that sort of moderate outlook and modern lifestyle. <br /> <br /> Maybe ideally, Garou would want some limited degree of isolation from mainstream society, kind of like the fundamentalist home schoolers but who believe in Gaia instead. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T11:21:33-07:00","id":1397116,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1129_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1129\" data-vbnamecard=\"1129\">Sergeant Brother</a> what you\u2019re describing with the law firm is probably how the Glass Walkers treat their Kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T12:14:42-07:00","id":1397122,"title":"","content":"In terms of kinfolk communities themselves, there is a spectrum. We can use that spectrum to create a range of kinfolk under more control to less control by the Garou.<br /> <br /> Kinfolk communities that are severely isolated from the world. Completely adopt the Garou worldview, and even their open activities reflect it within the needs of the Veil. Visitors there immediately know &quot;something is wrong.&quot; Emulates a lot of tropes in horror stories where the protagonists visit the place and immediately cross the threshold into horror as a result. Likely very rare in modern day, but could be present in very remote settings like northern Russia, Alaska, and Canada or isolated mountain communities that can be completely self sufficient. Best used in game to showcase antagonist factions or the more monstrous or alien aspects of Garou culture.<br /> <br /> Kinfolk communities mostly isolated from the world. Garou worldview incorporated into the community's culture, but an outside visitor could still believe there is nothing supernatural about the community. Many such communities hide as alternative fringe to the mainstream - hippie communes, survivalist homesteads, religious dissenters, cult compounds, etc. These communities emulate tropes from the folk horror genre. Movies and books like Wicker Man, Harvest Home, and Midsommar. Visitors to these communities know they aren't &quot;normal&quot;, but accept them as mundane. It would require investigation to determine &quot;something is wrong&quot;. These kinds of communities are probably a minority among kinfolk settlements, but represent a substantial amount of the &quot;conservative&quot; (or &quot;radical&quot; if more appropriate) view of each tribe's culture.<br /> <br /> Kinfolk communities divorced from the world. These communities appear normal at first glance, but divergences can be found if one looks close enough. Churches and schools have unusual texts that diverge from the mainstream, and there are many peculiar local celebrations and customs. If found, they can be disconcerting, but unless one spends much time there, they will simply go unnoticed. Kinfolk from these areas appear to fit in with the modern culture around them, but there is a conscious effort to hide what they &quot;really&quot; are. Many kinfolk communities make up this category, and it might be the one with the most plurality.<br /> <br /> Kinfolk communities integrated with the world. These communities are mixed kinfolk/human communities, and as a result make serious comprises with their Garou/Gaian worldview in order to co-exist safely with the outside world. Instead of controlling the dominant human institutions and propagating their views that way, they teach their values and lore in secret. Perhaps through &quot;volunteer groups&quot; and other private associations that can control membership. They may all belong to one church that is controlled by them as a cover. Many aspects of Garou society can either not be taught openly, or only taught once children reach a certain age in order to prevent inadvertent piercings of the Veil. Although the specifics of Garou culture are kept secret, these communities often reflect their values in ways amenable to the Flock. There are more of these types of Kinfolk communities in the modern world, and they are probably the default of most PCs.<br /> <br /> Kinfolk communities lost to the world. These communities are minority groups dominated by humans. Garou values are completely subverted by the dominant culture. They can only be taught as family secrets, although dedicated kinfolk families stay in touch with one another and support each other that way. Those that are in direct contact with the Garou can be expected to keep the faith. But families that are not in direct contact have a tendency to fall off the radar and become lost to the culture entirely. There is a paranoia among Garou and Kinfolk here about the Veil and losing kinfolk. Although the most &quot;open&quot; of all kinfolk communities, this means the Garou may be forced to use threats and intimidation to keep kinfolk within the fold. Probably the default community of must urban Garou and their kinfolk. Can also be found in rural kinfolk communities subsequently swallowed by suburbs.<br /> <br /> Lost kinfolk. These are not kinfolk communities at all, but kinfolk in human communities who have completely lost contact with the rest of the Garou Nation. Some kinfolk may still know of their heritage and cherish it, but fear losing the next generation. Other kinfolk know, but have rejected their heritage and seek complete absorbtion among humanity, often viewing their blood as &quot;cursed&quot; or &quot;tainted&quot; or otherwise undesirable. Other kinfolk have completely lost touch with their Garou roots. This is best used as background of Lost Cubs and Lunatics. This can also include families of Ronin that may know about werewolves, but are ignorant about Garou. Once rare, this now makes up a substantial part of the kinfolk population. More join every year, but many kinfolk family lines cease being kinfolk in future generations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T14:39:13-07:00","id":1397155,"title":"","content":"I'll only mention sexual violence to say that I've recently learned that it is the policy in some LARP groups to include within their rules that the concepts of 'rape' and 'sexual violence' are completely foreign within their IC universe and that the concepts are entirely absent both in theory and in practice.<br /> <br /> I know that's not going to be done people's preferred solution but I personally admire the choice to make a firm stance to create a safe environment for their players.<br /> <br /> Anyway returning to the main subject of this thread, I agree with what many people have been saying that kinfolk culture exists on a spectrum but is more akin to the relationship ancient warrior societies had between the warrior-priest class and the laborer-artisan class. Not slavery or servitude, but cultures that resemble pre-industrial societies in many respects. Isolated, insular, and firmly hierarchical with leadership by an elite religious and military class.<br /> <br /> I also think that Black Fox's post above makes a good point about the different sorts of kinfolk communities that would likely exist on a spectrum from entirely isolated to a concealed subculture.<br /> <br /> It personally makes me imagine a situation where one can explore a variety of septs with distinct garou-kinfolk communities. From the most isolated territories of rural backwoods, to communes vaguely known to the outside world, to communities masquerading as members of a larger culture whether in the form of entire small towns and villages or in the case of neighborhood and suburb groups.<br /> <br /> I would imagine that the Garou Nation considers most of its kinfolk to live communally in secret of hidden communities alongside traditional high tribes with the truly isolated and the human-presenting kinfolk of tribes such as the Bone Gnawers, Red Talons, and Glass Walkers being the minority. Of kenning kinfolk this may even be accurate. <br /> <br /> However I also imagine that callow kinfolk vastly outnumber their kenning counterparts and that for every group of kenning kinfolk in a small town in rural America claimed by a few high tribes, there are five or ten more groups of callow kinfolk that are living largely ordinary lives either ignoring or ignorant of their ancestry.<br /> <br /> The growth of the modern world and the defection of kinfolk is perhaps the most significant existential threat to the Garou Nation alongside that of Industrialization, Environmental Hazard, The Mad Weaver, and The Mad Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T15:08:50-07:00","id":1397160,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11637_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11637\" data-vbnamecard=\"11637\">Gryffon15</a> I agree with that choice. I like knowing I could play in a safe environment if I ever wanted to do that.<br /> <br /> Also, I agree with you about callow versus kenning Kinfolk. There are in all likelihood a lot of Kinfolk who either have no interest in being involved in the Garou Nation or are completely unaware of their heritage. (Though I would think the vast majority of callow Kinfolk wouldn\u2019t have any Gifts or special abilities beyond being able to have Garou children.)<br /> <br /> Would you recommend the W20 Kinfolk book? I\u2019m looking for some new WoD stuff to buy anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T15:39:51-07:00","id":1397164,"title":"","content":"If you can do so with economic safety, then I'd say that the W20 Kinfolk book is a really interesting read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T17:40:01-07:00","id":1397176,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m gonna get it. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T17:49:34-07:00","id":1397178,"title":"","content":"I recommend everyone pick up a copy of Monty Cook's CONSENT IN GAMING for a recommended read. It's only a dozen pages but well worth it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/288535/Consent-in-Gaming\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/4952/288535.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/288535/Consent-in-Gaming\" target=\"_blank\"> Consent in Gaming - Monte Cook Games | Numenera | The Strange | Cypher System | No Thank You, Evil! | Free Products | Invisible Sun | Your Best Game Ever | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/288535/Consent-in-Gaming\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/288535/Consent-in-Gaming </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Consent in Gaming - Tackle Mature Content with Confidence! From fending off an attack by bloodthirsty pirates to delving into dank caverns, </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T18:08:35-07:00","id":1397180,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m going to look into the Kinfolk book too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T19:03:49-07:00","id":1397194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1397178#post1397178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recommend everyone pick up a copy of Monty Cook's CONSENT IN GAMING for a recommended read. It's only a dozen pages but well worth it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/288535/Consent-in-Gaming\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...sent-in-Gaming</a></div> </div> </div> </div>This is also a free PDF, so you can avoid harming the players at your table with triggering topics without a financial cost to you or them. I had all my Mage players go through it and filled out what I was comfortable with as a Storyteller so they knew that certain topics were off the table and which ones I was going to focus on in the game.<br /> <br /> When filling out the Consent in Gaming PDF, be aware that you can add things later if you find them to be triggering or uncomfortable. That being said, if someone at your table is uncomfortable, please stop and make sure the game doesn't harm them.<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness games are fun--when we go to the levels and types of darkness we want.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T19:37:36-07:00","id":1397205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1397122#post1397122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyway, I like the breakdown you have there. How do you think that should be divided by Tribe. Some are obvious, with Glass Walker kinfolk living largely in the human world. Others are less obvious or more varied.<br /> <br /> i suspect that some of the more isolated communities could be targeted by the authorities, especially authorities that could be influenced or even just tipped off by influential Wyrm servants. \u201cHey, are these kids enrolled in school? Are those buildings up to code? Do you have permits for those guns/animals/etc.?\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T20:08:53-07:00","id":1397210,"title":"","content":"The Monty Cook book is a good thing to signal boost, 100% we folks should check it out.<br /> <br /> To Sergeant Brother's point though, yeah, I think the Garou Nation is great in that way to illustrate both how shadowy it can be and the world can be, because you've got really two branches here.<br /> <br /> Either the world doesn't notice, which has a dark ambience all its own. It's the gothic feeling of neglect, that certain people have been abandoned by society and the status quo, left to fend for themselves and to develop their own insular subcultures. It's also the punkish-ness of struggling to shout out and rouse the apathy surrounding you, something that the Garou Nation particularly struggles with when it, particularly its kinfolk, attempt to spread their message. <br /> <br /> Then you have the other side of the coin which is an analysis of how screwed up and dysfunctional elements of the Garou Nation are when you consider how they would interact with the contemporary west. Sure, we all know that garou are an isolationist theocratic semi-primitivist warrior culture. But it hits different when you've got CPS examing your kin's records. When a garou is pulled over and is incapable of producing legitimate identification, because he doesn't legally exist. When you have to hide your ritual practices not only to avoid the servants of the Wyrm; but ordinary curiosity, moral authorities, and religious groups.<br /> <br /> Nothing makes you realize quite how strange your circumstances have become like finding that you can no longer rely upon something that you would ordinarily take for granted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T21:16:26-07:00","id":1397222,"title":"","content":"In a game im running the First Returnefd Camazotz in ages Has a shadow lord host who Manages his kinfolk with a &quot;Spare the rod spoil the child&quot; Attitude forcing his daughter into a boarding school to keep her safe from Frenzys.<br /> <br /> And hes about to have his maid replaced and he did his best to find the old one a good husband.<br /> <br /> The new one is still learning the rules of her position.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T21:51:19-07:00","id":1397229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1397205#post1397205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, I like the breakdown you have there. How do you think that should be divided by Tribe. Some are obvious, with Glass Walker kinfolk living largely in the human world. Others are less obvious or more varied.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think all tribes can could find communities in all categories though some are more natural than others. Glass Walkers and urban Bone Gnawers would almost always have their kinfolk surrounded by humans. But there are certain things you can do to make your communities more secretive. I think one reason the Glass Walkers had the Wise Guys camp is not only is it a means for power, that the secretive nature of the criminal subcommunity would make it easier to be openly Garou within it while shielding it from outsiders. I think other secretive subcommunities would also serve the same purpose - fraternal organizations, certain kinds of ethnic minority neighborhoods, radical political groups, controversial organizations - anything that would deter most people from socializing with members, but allow them to occupy a certain amount of physical space. Mundane humanity would thus see their separation from the rest of the city as &quot;normal&quot; because that would be expected for that groups. That could lead to an isolated community (kinfolk oasis) in the middle of mundane humanity.<br /> <br /> I find Silver Fangs interesting because I think they occupy both extremes a lot. They have members that bred with human nobility, and thus have members well connected to humanity. But I also imagine they have small isolated communities in the swamps and forests of Siberia or what have you that still represent Garou nobility (and high pure breed), but never interbred with human nobility.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> i suspect that some of the more isolated communities could be targeted by the authorities, especially authorities that could be influenced or even just tipped off by influential Wyrm servants. \u201cHey, are these kids enrolled in school? Are those buildings up to code? Do you have permits for those guns/animals/etc.?\u201d </div> </div> </div>I suspect the smaller communities are so remote that most government bureaucrats never touch them. What local enforcement there is usually comes from institutions the kinfolk themselves have people in power like the County Sheriff. Agents of the Wyrm could go after them, assuming they identify them, but it'd truly be a waste of most resources in most cases. The big exception is when great amounts of money could be made from nearby natural resources extraction. Once enough money is at stake, the wheels will get greased.<br /> <br /> But like all things, one can imagine a lot of different scenarios.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T22:00:53-07:00","id":1397231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1397222#post1397222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a game im running the First Returnefd Camazotz in ages Has a shadow lord host who Manages his kinfolk with a &quot;Spare the rod spoil the child&quot; Attitude forcing his daughter into a boarding school to keep her safe from Frenzys.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think institutions like boarding schools, orphanages, fraternal orders, charitable foundations, religious orders, local heritage or genealogical groups, and certain hobby organizations would be used by kinfok a lot. Anything that can be used to segregate people, create strong ties among participants, and exclude others (non-kinfolk) from their activities yet appear normal to outsiders would prove very useful.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T22:21:19-07:00","id":1397233,"title":"","content":"On to the next category of control - the Extended Family/Large Neighborhood category.<br /> <br /> If immediate family meant control like a strict parent in a traditional society, then I think this one is like the family patriarch or matriarch. A grandparent with influence over their own adult children and also their grandchildren and maybe more. Another example might be the influence of a trusted religious leader in their congregation - someone who could secure the blessings of the spirits or Gaia for their extended family. This would also be the equivalent of high amounts of the Kinfolk background which give 20 or 50 kinfolk over to the PC to control. (Again, certain benefits may need to have Allies, Contacts, or Resources background mechanically than just the Kinfolk background, but everything would be tied to it being Kinfolk that is the origin of that.)<br /> <br /> I think defining the scope is easy. Detailing the amount of control is a bit harder. While not having the direct authority of a parent over his children, I do think this amounts to &quot;a head of the family&quot;.<br /> <br /> I think in terms of finances and requesting resources and service, the Garou is about the same as immediate family, but perhaps being less burdensome and more indirect. Instead of taking direct control of resources, the Garou would inform this extended the group of the amount of resources needed, and it'd be up to the group to figure it out for themselves and pony it up. They'd distribute the burden as fairly as they could and then turn it over. So the end result is the same, but it seems a little less oppressive.<br /> <br /> In terms of controlling marriage or mating of kinfolk in this group, I think it'd be more of a veto over anything she'd find objectionable. Perhaps done in a way that the expectation is that the kinfolk obtain &quot;her blessing&quot;, but if that is not provided then it simply isn't done and the community is ready to ostracize the objecting kinfolk. If the Garou actually wants to pair someone in this group as a mate to some other kinfolk or Garou, it is probably done via social pressure instead of just arranging it herself. The Garou may be thwarted her, but a highly skilled social Garou can probably make it happen. At this group, relations are distant enough it may be possible for a Garou to seek her own mate from the group. As long as the consanguinity is accepted by the Garou's tribe or sept, I think it would hold. Obviously this is more acceptable in some tribes more than others. I don't think Garou could override any objection other Garou in their tribe have at that in principle. But if the tribe overall is acceptable of that, then it happens.<br /> <br /> Because we're still in the mechanics of Backgrounds zone, I think a lot of the control is the same. But how it is exercised is different, and the more important for Garou to have higher social skills than relying just on the authority of their position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T22:28:51-07:00","id":1397237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1397229#post1397229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think all tribes can could find communities in all categories though some are more natural than others. Glass Walkers and urban Bone Gnawers would almost always have their kinfolk surrounded by humans. But there are certain things you can do to make your communities more secretive. I think one reason the Glass Walkers had the Wise Guys camp is not only is it a means for power, that the secretive nature of the criminal subcommunity would make it easier to be openly Garou within it while shielding it from outsiders. I think other secretive subcommunities would also serve the same purpose - fraternal organizations, certain kinds of ethnic minority neighborhoods, radical political groups, controversial organizations - anything that would deter most people from socializing with members, but allow them to occupy a certain amount of physical space. Mundane humanity would thus see their separation from the rest of the city as &quot;normal&quot; because that would be expected for that groups. That could lead to an isolated community (kinfolk oasis) in the middle of mundane humanity.<br /> <br /> I find Silver Fangs interesting because I think they occupy both extremes a lot. They have members that bred with human nobility, and thus have members well connected to humanity. But I also imagine they have small isolated communities in the swamps and forests of Siberia or what have you that still represent Garou nobility (and high pure breed), but never interbred with human nobility.<br /> <br /> I suspect the smaller communities are so remote that most government bureaucrats never touch them. What local enforcement there is usually comes from institutions the kinfolk themselves have people in power like the County Sheriff. Agents of the Wyrm could go after them, assuming they identify them, but it'd truly be a waste of most resources in most cases. The big exception is when great amounts of money could be made from nearby natural resources extraction. Once enough money is at stake, the wheels will get greased.<br /> <br /> But like all things, one can imagine a lot of different scenarios.</div> </div> </div> </div>Garou with access to lots of money, either from businesses for modern Garou or noble families for the more old fashioned, could find ways to make communities which were both ideologically pure and yet not underprivileged. For example, kinfolk boarding schools and summer camps for Silver Fang or Shadow Lord (just two examples) kinfolk. They could be raised in a way to protect them from dangerous elements of modern society, but also given important knowledge about the modern world and put in a situation to make good connections later on. That is the best of both worlds in a way.<br /> <br /> As for human authorities, I think it\u2019s a good tactic for Pentex, for example, because it\u2019s relatively low risk and low cost and would cause the kinfolk a huge headache on the tax payer\u2019s dime. If you have some Pentex executive with access to a politician or news network, it would be extremely easy to create a storm of negative attention for some isolated kinfolk community. Think of the news headlines - extremist cult compound found in the woods. They don\u2019t educate their children. They are child molesters. They are Neo-Nazis, Satanists, or some other very unpopular and feared ideology. They are amassing guns. They are terrorists. The list could go on. The kinfolk community might not be anything close to any of that, or maybe the reports can take a few quirks of the community and exaggerate them, but it doesn\u2019t actually matter. I could easily see it turning into a Waco situation even without Pentex pulling any strings to encourage persecution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T04:50:39-07:00","id":1397269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1397237#post1397237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for human authorities, I think it\u2019s a good tactic for Pentex, for example, because it\u2019s relatively low risk and low cost and would cause the kinfolk a huge headache on the tax payer\u2019s dime. If you have some Pentex executive with access to a politician or news network, it would be extremely easy to create a storm of negative attention for some isolated kinfolk community. Think of the news headlines - extremist cult compound found in the woods. They don\u2019t educate their children. They are child molesters. They are Neo-Nazis, Satanists, or some other very unpopular and feared ideology. They are amassing guns. They are terrorists. The list could go on. The kinfolk community might not be anything close to any of that, or maybe the reports can take a few quirks of the community and exaggerate them, but it doesn\u2019t actually matter. I could easily see it turning into a Waco situation even without Pentex pulling any strings to encourage persecution.</div> </div> </div> </div>The other part of this is that the kinfolk community will have a sept and caern of some sort attached/linked to it. Thus going after the kinfolk may force the garou to brake cover to protect them, and thus expose them selves as targets. Also thinking longer term - take out the kinfolk community, and in a generation the septwill be a lot weaker - due to no new garou been born - and the caern will be an available target to take out.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T07:35:32-07:00","id":1397288,"title":"","content":"Agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1129_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1129\" data-vbnamecard=\"1129\">Sergeant Brother</a>. Defo boarding schools and summer camps, especially for Silver Fangs, Fianna and possibly Shadow Lords. I could also see a (fictional) school like Andover or Exeter being used by multiple tribes or possibly even the entire Nation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T07:42:10-07:00","id":1397291,"title":"","content":"Consent In Gaming is great!!! Especially the Checklist \ud83d\ude0a\ud83d\ude0a\ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T08:13:16-07:00","id":1397295,"title":"","content":"how much influence would Persuasion pluss a good Social pool give parents over their children on things like<br /> <br /> <br /> 'Enter this Career'<br /> <br /> 'Marry this person'<br /> <br /> 'dont leave town'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T08:36:33-07:00","id":1397298,"title":"","content":"None, if their children are PCs.<br /> <br /> We\u2019re talking about Garou influence over Kinfolk, but I guess an attempt by a Garou parent to convince her NPC Kinfolk child to do or not do something would be resolved by a Social dice roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T10:41:07-07:00","id":1397326,"title":"","content":"a kinfolk boarding school sounds like a target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T11:10:05-07:00","id":1397334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1397326#post1397326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a kinfolk boarding school sounds like a target.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anywhere that kinfolk or Garou are concentrated is a target, but a boarding school or something similar has advantages. One thing is that it is respectable. The FBI aren\u2019t going to raid a boarding school, or if they do it\u2019s going to require a lot more use of political clout to get them to do it. A boarding school can have security and in fact is a good central location that can be guarded by Garou or spirits. If the boarding school gets attacked, the attackers will be investigated by the police, not the boarding school itself. The staff can keep a close eye on the kid\u2019s to notice a first change and minimize the associated risks.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s likely safer than an off the grid compound, maybe even more secret than one too. It\u2019s also probably safer than just letting kinfolk kids live integrated with normal human kids.<br /> <br /> I can see it now - Professor Albrecht\u2019s School for Gifted Youngsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T12:33:48-07:00","id":1397350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1397334#post1397334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anywhere that kinfolk or Garou are concentrated is a target, but a boarding school or something similar has advantages. One thing is that it is respectable. The FBI aren\u2019t going to raid a boarding school, or if they do it\u2019s going to require a lot more use of political clout to get them to do it. A boarding school can have security and in fact is a good central location that can be guarded by Garou or spirits. If the boarding school gets attacked, the attackers will be investigated by the police, not the boarding school itself. The staff can keep a close eye on the kid\u2019s to notice a first change and minimize the associated risks.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s likely safer than an off the grid compound, maybe even more secret than one too. It\u2019s also probably safer than just letting kinfolk kids live integrated with normal human kids.<br /> <br /> I can see it now - Professor Albrecht\u2019s School for Gifted Youngsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly!!! Agree with everything you just said. And you must be psychic \ud83d\ude0a. My sophomore year RA\u2019s last name was Albrecht.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T12:55:40-07:00","id":1397357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1397350#post1397350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly!!! Agree with everything you just said. And you must be psychic \ud83d\ude0a. My sophomore year RA\u2019s last name was Albrecht.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you a Silver Fang? \ud83d\ude27","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T13:53:42-07:00","id":1397369,"title":"","content":"Ohhhhhhh. The Silver Fang King.<br /> <br /> Right. I forgot.<br /> <br /> No \ud83d\ude0a. I was being literal (and a little silly). But I am drawn to the Silver Fangs as well as the Fianna and the Black Furies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T14:43:30-07:00","id":1397383,"title":"","content":"It's a pretty easy target. Kill everyone, blame a group of students, cite the unhealthy alleged practices of the school as something that pushed the kids over the edge. <br /> <br /> or you could blame... eco terrorists. <br /> <br /> youve got a lot of eggs in one basket that cant justify too much security<br /> You have many means to kill a lot of kids fast<br /> you have the media at your disposal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T15:03:20-07:00","id":1397388,"title":"","content":"If people would like to continue discussion about how kinfolk communities could be targeted by PENTEX or other forces of the Wyrm, and how the Garou could defend them (or the Kinfolk themselves), then I ask you start another thread for that discussion. It could easily hijack this thread which I'd like to concentrate on the original topic - how Garou can control Kinfolk, and how to implement that in the game.<br /> <br /> I think it's a topic sufficiently large that it could swallow this thread whole and crowd out actual discussion of its topic.<br /> <br /> There's been some good discussion here, and I'd like to keep things on topic to keep building on it. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T15:26:29-07:00","id":1397394,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> both boarding schools and summer camps are typically built in rural areas or near small towns and would be ideal for housing and controlling Kinfolk who would be at or near the age of their First Change.<br /> <br /> Not sure if this is relevant, but I had an idea for a Black Fury Kinfolk who undergoes her First Change when she finds out her non-Kin boyfriend has been cheating on her and accidentally kills him. Unfortunately, it turns out her bf is a scion of the Boston Milliner family...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T19:07:22-07:00","id":1397421,"title":"","content":"I agree that things like boarding schools, summer camps, even scouting troops, youth groups, and certain athletic camps could all be great ways to induct young kinfolk into Garou values and watch over for potential First Change Garou. And they even work for urban Garou who dwell among many humans and might not have been informed when they were very young. They make good friends because they seem &quot;normal&quot; yet allow children to be taken away for extended time periods without other contact or supervision besides the people who oversee those activities. Depending on how much time is available, they could introduce things either slowly or fast, allow them to process any potential shock of revelation under supervision.<br /> <br /> I expect conveniences like email and cell phones would have to be removed, blocked, or clandestinely monitored, but that can easily be done.<br /> <br /> For adults, I think organizations like fraternal organizations, local history/genealogical/heritage societies would also work. Non-kinfolk can be secretly blackballed from joining while unknowing kinfolk can be isolated and properly instructed.<br /> <br /> I think Bone Gnawers are at a disadvantage because they lack the resources to create and maintain these kind of organizations, though they could piggy back on those done by other tribes who compensate with &quot;scholarships&quot; or charity. But I think for the most part, we need to think of alternative methods of instruction more appropriate to the feel or theme of the tribe. Perhaps the use of urban legends, and informal institutions found on the street. There may also be things like homeless shelters, delinquent youth groups, juvenile correction halls (or outreach programs), orphanages or foster care networks that are effectively coopted or controlled. And since Bonegnawers may have a lot of runaway kids living on the streets, there could be certain child gangs or Fagin like mentors who can do the same.<br /> <br /> I think developing institutions and organizations like these that help inform and protect (slash control) kinfolk make excellent additions to chronicle settings and PC backgrounds.<br /> <br /> = = = = = =<br /> I also use sexual or romantic urgings/emotions of Garou to produce the First Change. I also think they make great Forced/Banned Transformation flaws too!.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 06-18-2020, 10:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T19:23:01-07:00","id":1397425,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> I agree. The Bone Gnawers may also have ties to gang culture in urban areas (though maybe not so much in more rural areas such as Appalachia). And thanks \ud83d\ude0a. I think I\u2019m gonna use the idea I told you about as a Prelude if I ever play Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T10:35:21-07:00","id":1397548,"title":"","content":"Glass walkers likely offer the best conditions for their human kinfolk with great high paying jobs that make their kin want to stay around (hurray nepotism!) They can even have cool things like Dies Ultimae and trust in their kin not to shoot em in the back. but their wolf kinfolk largely live in enclosures. <br /> <br /> Dies ultimae (or however it's spelt) is cool AF, but you couldnt do anything like them with other tribes on a comparative scale, and the glass walkers are a small tribe. <br /> <br /> Even giving kinfolk guns to defend the sept has a good share of problems. You can't completely trust the kin, using kin that way is dishonourable, and you're justifying an armed attack when your cult-compound is so well armed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T23:26:42-07:00","id":1397631,"title":"","content":"A Tribe that has a close connection to its kinfolk and doesn't mistreat them should be able to let them have guns and the ability to use them without being afraid of betrayal. In rural or wilderness areas of the USA, an isolated community is likely to have lots of guns. It might be odd if they weren't heavily armed. In other nations, having a lot of guns is going to be harder, though even in Western Europe where guns are rarer, people living in rural communities still often have rifles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T03:39:09-07:00","id":1397647,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1129_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1129\" data-vbnamecard=\"1129\">Sergeant Brother</a> maybe even guns with silver bullets in case of a Black Spiral Dancer attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T06:48:42-07:00","id":1397715,"title":"","content":"There's a big difference between &quot;What actually happens&quot; and &quot;what we can make you think happened&quot;. <br /> <br /> Yes, you can have a rural community that's well armed. That's normal in some places. But it's pretty easy to convince most people that those guys were wackos (or Wacos). You tell the ATF you think they're stockpiling illegal weapons, you tell the human rights charities in your pocket that they're abusing people. You can file a missing person's report where someone went near the place and was never seen again. When you actually look at the place, you can likely find obscure religious items denoting that it's a cult. There's just loads of ways you can turn a bunch of weirdos living among nature into a vicious organization. I think a lot of people will <i>want </i>to believe you're dealing with a sensational cult. The Garou either stick with their kinfolk or move to protect the Caern; They're gonna sacrifice something, just because the guns drew the attention of the police and media. <br /> <br /> (you could also just chuck bigger amounts of soldiers at the sept but that risks the veil) <br /> <br /> But also if Garou give their kinfolk access to a lot of quality silver weapons, what's to stop a kinfolk from going postal? Especially if we throw a vampire's dominate into the mix. The less you give your kinfolk, the better. If you give them a few simple bolt action hunting rifles, how do they stop serious attackers with numbers and semi-autos? <br /> <br /> From the garou point of view, the less their kinfolk do (other than breeding, providing income, and servitude) the better. Letting kinfolk take up some militaristic function is a threat physically and a threat to the honour of garou who pride themselves on being Gaia's warriors. What's your existence to you if someone you thought of as weaker can do a job just as good as you? Do people need your services if they can do things themselves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T07:19:49-07:00","id":1397724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1397715#post1397715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the garou point of view, the less their kinfolk do (other than breeding, providing income, and servitude) the better. Letting kinfolk take up some militaristic function is a threat physically and a threat to the honour of garou who pride themselves on being Gaia's warriors. What's your existence to you if someone you thought of as weaker can do a job just as good as you? Do people need your services if they can do things themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's actually the opposite, the kinfolk do a LOT of work the garou simply cannot do and that is by design. Remember, even a philodox with 3 rage triggers the Curse on 30% of people around them. That means things like buying guns, getting military/police training and such are out of the question for most garou. But for kinfolk, those are common paths to take and they can share their knowledge and influence that way.<br /> <br /> The garou pride isn't really as much over the ability to fight as it is the way they've been empowered by Gaia to fight. Kinfolk cannot change forms, cannot go to the umbra, cannot use gifts and cannot use Rage. No matter how good fighters they are, garou are gifted by Gaia to be always better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T09:13:31-07:00","id":1397750,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar110_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"110\" data-vbnamecard=\"110\">Ana Mizuki</a> very good point","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T12:12:49-07:00","id":1397785,"title":"","content":"Why would garou want guns/military training? They have their forebears for that (I mean they learn from eachother, ancestor spirits and all that are secondary) A society as militaristic as the garou doesn't need outside help for <i>training</i>. (this is part fact, part garou pride) <br /> <br /> <br /> I'd argue that silver loaded firearms have really closed the gap between Kinfolk and Garou. Silver isn't that expensive nowadays, so if you have the technical skill to craft the bullets, you're ready to go. If he's not suffering from delerium, a kinfolk shooter <i>with a matchlock </i>loaded with silver has a fair chance of defeating an unarmed Garou (I'd give him 30% odds of winning in most Terrain) A Kinfolk with a semi automatic rifle of sufficient size has a 70% chance of winning, and a kinfolk with a general purpose machinegun loaded with silver has a 70% chance of annihilating an entire pack. Sure, rage might come in handy if a werewolf is shooting back at five guys, but it isn't really a huge advantage if he's shooting back at one. <br /> Garou largely get by because of enemy ignorance/lack of appropriate tools/delirium and the fact that most of their fights happen in the umbra where brawls occur and shootouts are rare. The best thing for Garou as warriors in a war with guns is that they've got a whole load of utility options that normal people don't have, letting them pick battles better and get the jump on others. But if kinfolk got the jump on Garou instead... <br /> <br /> So many Silver bullets close to home would make Garou-me nervous. I'd like to think I'd be a nice garou, but I don't know, I remembered instances of being a prick in my teens and I don't know how my thinking would change being in a survival cult (I was quite the cynic but I woulda loved to be the special kid that did well and got special privelages so...) Maybe Normal gun's would be fine but a weapon specifically designed to kill my kind? So many? Around me? Then we add a siege mentality, hear stories of abuse and traitors... <br /> <br /> Kinfolk should be for mundane stuff, like fetching something from the store, getting stuff posted, cooking, giving my wife the constant backrubs she needs to placate her ferocious rage, picking cotton... <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T12:36:44-07:00","id":1397790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1397785#post1397785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would garou want guns/military training? They have their forebears for that (I mean they learn from eachother, ancestor spirits and all that are secondary) A society as militaristic as the garou doesn't need outside help for <i>training</i>. (this is part fact, part garou pride)<br /> <br /> --------------<br /> <br /> Kinfolk should be for mundane stuff, like fetching something from the store, getting stuff posted, cooking, giving my wife the constant backrubs she needs to placate her ferocious rage, picking cotton...</div> </div> </div> </div>Because garou aren't vampires, each generation comes from the local human(and wolf) stock. And most only live to 40 at BEST. Sure, there are those raised in isolation, but there are many garou born to distant kinfolk who grew up in modern or so culture. Besides, there are two city tribes whose whole thing is that they adapt to human cultures and take from them. Glass Walkers don't even have mentors since they see them as old fashioned. Even tribes who aren't in cities still adapt to guns unless they are intentionally very isolated.<br /> <br /> As for kinfolk jobs, remember the Curse. Most garou are too scary for humans to be near. This means things like land-rights,money, tools, housing,etc. are all on kinfolk. They are the contacts in local councils, politicians, park rangers and such. Basically, without them, the garou couldn't exist as they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T13:22:26-07:00","id":1397803,"title":"","content":"So <i>a few </i>kinfolk are important enough not to abuse. Or maybe they are. A lot of cults have people with important assets to the cult and they pool them in for the good of the cult... <hr /><br /> I watched this today <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SbMzYRMxIvA\" data-code=\"SbMzYRMxIvA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/SbMzYRMxIvA/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I feel it somewhat relevant, somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T13:31:28-07:00","id":1397806,"title":"","content":"I think many rural kinfolk communities in the US will &quot;heavily&quot; armed because that is often the norm. They'll have sidearms for self defense and rifles for hunting and sportsmanship. They may even have heavier arms because some people find it fun to set up a target range and shoot them. It's simply part of the outdoor culture of the United States. Many rural kinfolk are going to be hikers, campers, hunters, and fishermen. That could be different in other countries which have a different outdoor culture.<br /> <br /> I don't think they'll deviate much from the non-kinfolk population in this. And I don't see why the Garou would object. They would want their kinfolk to defend themselves if needed. Some, like the Get of Fenris, will probably insist on it.<br /> <br /> What I think the Garou would object to is the presence of silver in their communities especially any silver somehow not known or controlled. (There could always be some kind of justification for a known and monitored stockpile of silver, such as protection in case Black Spiral Dancers attack).<br /> <br /> I don't think Garou only view kinfolk as fit for some kind of menial labor. Kinfolk are too great an asset to be used like that. Highly skilled kinfolk would not only be preferred as mates, but they would want their kinfolk communities to be self-supporting and able to productively contribute to Garou in terms of providing finances, equipment, and skills. The Kinfolk background is primarily for routine or mundane help, but many of the Allies and Contacts a Garou will have will also be Kinfolk but using that mechanic instead. Garou would want their kinfolk to be skilled enough to be physicians, sheriff officers, enlist in the armed forces, lawyers &amp; judges, and many other skilled or prestigious professions because that will protect those communities and help the Garou.<br /> <br /> And while I think most Garou will use other Garou as their teachers. if there is truly an excellent local expert in whatever ability in a kinfolk, I don't think they'd refuse to make use of it. And before the First Change happens, a Garou's early preparation will often be from adult kinfolk instructing them how to do things. One of the benefits of truly having a kinfolk community of several hundred people is that kinfolk adults can adequately prepare pre-Change cubs in skills they will need after they change. Those kids won't have to wait until their First Change to pick up skills in Survival, Firearms, Stealth, and other skills. They can learn them in school, in Boy Scout troops, in family camping trips, on the farm and family owned businesses, and extracurricular activities. They'll have an advantage over cubs who don't come from those backgrounds, and thus will more quickly become Cliaths and be useful to the Nation.<br /> <br /> I see sometimes in online games that Kinfolk PCs want to be ersatz Garou, and I don't see Garou wanting that. They're not packmates and they don't replace Garou. When supernatural threats arise, the Garou want the Kinfolk out of the way and in a safe place just like adults want children to be safe inside the home if something dangerous is happening outside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T14:42:45-07:00","id":1397820,"title":"","content":"The point of the kinfolk is that they do most of the mundane and costly work so their garou relatives can go on spirit quests and fight their war. They are basically the backbone of the Nation, hence the first kinfolk book title being Unsung Heroes. They are not put down cultists or slaves, they are the reason why most non-city tribes can exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T19:08:52-07:00","id":1397873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1397820#post1397820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point of the kinfolk is that they do most of the mundane and costly work so their garou relatives can go on spirit quests and fight their war. They are basically the backbone of the Nation, hence the first kinfolk book title being Unsung Heroes. They are not put down cultists or slaves, they are the reason why most non-city tribes can exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! Exactly \ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T19:51:00-07:00","id":1397880,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think that Garou would want kinfolk to have arsenals or silver bullets, because those are way too specific in their anti-Garou capacity as well as being expensive and suspicious of discovered. Mostly, danger to kinfolk wouldn\u2019t come from werewolves anyway. There may be a few magazines of silver ammo around for emergencies, and he\u2019s by highly trusted kinfolk, but it wouldn\u2019t be standard issue for the kinfolk communities.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, having a semi-automatic rifle at hand for every adult kinfolk in an isolated community shouldn\u2019t be that unusual in a country wear firearms can be readily accessed. Nor should it bother Garou who aren\u2019t really mean to their kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T21:41:02-07:00","id":1397894,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1129_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1129\" data-vbnamecard=\"1129\">Sergeant Brother</a> what about Black Spiral Dancers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T00:48:17-07:00","id":1397910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1397894#post1397894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1129_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1129\" data-vbnamecard=\"1129\">Sergeant Brother</a> what about Black Spiral Dancers?</div> </div> </div> </div>If BSD attack a Gaian kinfolk community, their chances of survival are probably low even with silver arsenals. Most enemies who would present a threat to the kinfolk wouldn't be BSD's, but other servants of the Wyrm or their pawns. Though, it's certainly possible that a kinfolk community could all be heavily armed with guns with silver bullets - though it would probably make a lot of Garou nervous, especially since most foes won't be Garou, it will be expensive, and it could pose a threat to other Garou.<br /> <br /> I would imagine that some kinfolk would arm themselves with silver weaponry, but that it wouldn't be that common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T01:08:48-07:00","id":1397913,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1129_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1129\" data-vbnamecard=\"1129\">Sergeant Brother</a> yes, but the Impergium was enforced with silver. I\u2019m far from an expert in military tactics, but if Kinfolk have both numerical superiority and silver bullets, couldn\u2019t they fend off an attacking BSD pack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T10:16:11-07:00","id":1398004,"title":"","content":"The chance of a BSD attack on a Caern is a lot lower than anyone else attacking a caern. And if BSD did attack, there's a chance they'll do it in the umbra. <br /> <br /> Normal bullets can still hurt, wound and kill BSD, they're just less effective, and they're slightly superior in terms of fighting formor and humans. The thing is, nobody's going to invade a caern unless they're pretty sure they'll win or they think their sacrifice is absolutely neccessary. Hoping for the best, the garou have something hidden up their sleeve, and the BSD's in the Assault have demanded their formor and paramilitary backup not use silver (For fear of betrayal). <br /> <br /> You are more likely to loose a caern with silver equiped kinfolk. If one of them goes around shooting (Either because of dominate or retaliation of abuse or because someone made them a special offer) and does some serious damage, they will set the stage for that aformentioned Wyrm assault. A small caern might literally be held by just a pack, so that gunman could get a royal flush and let the Wyrm walk right in. Someone going postal without silver likely won't do enough damage to encourage an attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T19:33:14-07:00","id":1398101,"title":"","content":"WoD tends to give massive advantages to offense and werewolves are insanely powerful. If a group of BSD\u2019s conduct a surprise attack on a kinfolk community, then in all likelihood not even silver bullets will save them. I\u2019m not saying that no kinfolk would ever have silver, groups like the Dies Ultimae should, but it should be more of an exception than the rule with most kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T20:35:41-07:00","id":1398108,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1129_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1129\" data-vbnamecard=\"1129\">Sergeant Brother</a> good point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T23:06:34-07:00","id":1398129,"title":"","content":"Before I get to the idea of Garou being appointed &quot;guardian&quot; to kinfolk, I want to discuss the general status of Kinfolk within a sept's protectorate that do not have an immediate Garou who is somehow acting as a pater familias to them. This should be the status of most kinfolk within the Garou Nation. They don't have an obvious Garou who is closely related to them.<br /> <br /> So in lieu of an individual Garou, that falls to the sept leadership. What can they command these kinfolk to do within the boundaries of Garou law? They must be able to do something, but it must fall far less than someone's father, brother, or other relative can do.<br /> <br /> I admit I'm not sure how to proceed. Still digesting this.<br /> <br /> I'll repeat - this is not to talk about appointing a &quot;guardian&quot; or similar role to do so. I'd like to talk about that later and figure out the mechanics of it. This is just about what the Garou as a whole - likely through their sept leadership - can do to just any nearby kinfolk. We're now outside the Kinfolk Background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T07:00:40-07:00","id":1398178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1397237#post1397237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou with access to lots of money, either from businesses for modern Garou or noble families for the more old fashioned, could find ways to make communities which were both ideologically pure and yet not underprivileged. For example, kinfolk boarding schools and summer camps for Silver Fang or Shadow Lord (just two examples) kinfolk. They could be raised in a way to protect them from dangerous elements of modern society, but also given important knowledge about the modern world and put in a situation to make good connections later on. That is the best of both worlds in a way.</div> </div> </div> </div>A great book on the constructed wilderness and social class reinforcement in summer camps is: <a href=\"https://www.ubcpress.ca/the-nurture-of-nature\" target=\"_blank\">The Nurture of Nature: Childhood, Antimodernism, and Ontario Summer Camps, 1920-55</a>. The whole time reading this I was taking note to flesh out the Silver Fang Protectorate I've been writing up for the region. It talks, not just, about the elite camps, but does mention some of the camps for less affluent kids too. Several of the camps still exist, including <a href=\"https://keewaydin.org/\" target=\"_blank\">Keeywadin</a>, <a href=\"https://www.taylorstattencamps.com/camp-ahmek-for-boys/\" target=\"_blank\">Camp Ahmek</a>, and <a href=\"http://camptemagami.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Camp Temagami</a> (for boys), and <a href=\"https://www.taylorstattencamps.com/camp-wapomeo-for-girls/\" target=\"_blank\">Camp Wapomeo</a> (for girls).<br /> <br /> And it would not just be the forces of the Wyrm campers (and staff) would have to contend with, depending on divisive the Garou Nation is in a specific game, there could be conflict with other groups. In the specific regions of the aforementioned camps, this would be a useful, though a bit dated, read: <a href=\"https://books.google.com/books/about/The_Temagami_Experience.html?id=jJpwQgAACAAJ\" target=\"_blank\">The Temagami experience : recreation, resources, and aboriginal rights in the northern Ontario wilderness</a>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T16:23:23-07:00","id":1398253,"title":"","content":"I definitely think that the question of how the Garou Nation deals with those kinfolk who do not have the benefit of a &quot;garou ambassador&quot; of sorts, those who have either suffered the tragedy of losing their garou kin to battle or (even worse) have suffered the tragedy of not bearing any garou this generation.<br /> <br /> While I do imagine that such groups would often try to reach out to their nearest living garou relative, it's possible that no such figure exists or that they would be beyond the group's reach, all too possible as the war rages and the kinfolk population continues to outstrip the garou minority by leaps and bounds.<br /> <br /> So from there what I imagine happening is that Kenning Kinfolk are often forced to make a choice of two options and from there to balance their obligations to *at least* two-three different areas. They must first choose to stay within the Nation as a group, which I imagine is a regular choice for those raised within the Nation, yet without a direct garou tie I can see some deciding to up-sticks.<br /> <br /> Assuming however that they remain within the Garou Nation as kenning kinfolk; I see them tied between their loyalties to each other, their sept, their tribe, and potentially any remaining packmates of their final garou who may feel obligated to offer stewardship.<br /> <br /> Naturally different tribal cultures will lead to different reactions and qualities but let me break down my logic.<br /> <br /> First the kinfolk must determine how they function as a sub-culture within the Nation. They must determine the needs of their membership and how their spiritual, martial, and managerial needs are to be addressed. The latter is likely the easiest as most kinfolk probably already had matriarchs, patriarchs, or elders who worked alongside the family garou. These are now likely to be the clan/band leaders. They must then determine how to achieve their other needs. Some might begin to create their own martial and spiritual practices if cut off from the Nation, but most will likely seek out Garou and here begins the balancing act. Who to go to? They're likely going to be inclined to find a suitable member of their own tribe, yet they are somewhat restricted by the dangers of leaving their local sept territory. They might represent an important resource bloc for the local garou, who may not feel comfortable simply letting them go. Yet they aren't likely to feel comfortable dictating to them either...<br /> <br /> Kinfolk families make up unspeakably important resources to the Garou. They provide material, logistics, and support as well as being absolutely vital for creating the next generation. This creates a strong incentive for septs to want to keep them close. I imagine that at the best of times the sept will put forward respected and honorable stewards to serve as regents for the family until they bear a garou of their own, or perhaps a quick marriage is made between a garou of the kinfolk's tribe.<br /> <br /> Yet what happens if the sept does not have a suitable member of the garou's own tribe or the kinfolk won't recognize a strange garou's authority over them? Trouble. At this point the kinfolk may attempt to leave or remain as a difficult to control subculture which the sept leadership likely will not tolerate. They will need to toe the line or leave and sometimes leaving is not an option, either to the Garou or the kinfolk.<br /> <br /> These cases I see as being one of the most prime sources of recruitment for tribes such as the Bone Gnawers, Glass Walkers, and *especially* the Children of Gaia. The former tribes have lost their pure breed and as such can welcome any newcomer while the latter tribe I imagine as having a significant population for a few key reasons.<br /> <br /> Their willingness to tolerate all gaian tribes, their relatively liberal style of government, and their absolute devotion to the ideals of purity and unity within the Nation. They may be an isolated kinfolk family's greatest chance for fair representation amongst Garou Society and as such I can see many kinfolk who cannot return to the territories of Garou of their own tribe flocking to them.<br /> <br /> That all said, I also think that the matter of tribe is extremely important as generally, a kinfolk group can expect to seek out another family of the same tribe and be welcomed as brothers and sisters under the protection of the latter group's living garou. The tribes are vast extended families that provide commonalities of culture for their members to seek out and be comforted by.<br /> <br /> Tribes also provide a safety net for uncertain kinfolk groups. Worst case scenario, if news reached the tribe in foreign septs that their kinfolk are at risk of becoming domineered or forcibly assimilated by other garou, the tribe may well come calling to claim their kinfolk, as many of them will see as their Gaia given rite.<br /> <br /> What I mean to say by all of this is that in most instances I imagine that the most common reaction of an isolated kinfolk group as to welcome a garou of the same tribe and sept into their number. Failing that they may seek out the safety of the Children of Gaia or call out to the tribemates further afield.<br /> <br /> However in these dark times where lives are perhaps the most important resource of all, there is much potential for conflict to be had simply by one garou deciding that their claim to or need of a kinfolk is superior to another's...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T22:00:22-07:00","id":1398287,"title":"","content":"While I think some Garou kinfolk may be at the &quot;margins&quot; Garou society, and torn between continuity with traditions and losing themselves with mundane humanity, I am thinking more of kinfolk who are well entrenched with Garou society - say in an exclusively kinfolk community with many Garou traditions - but simply don't have a Garou directly over them.<br /> <br /> In a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1332580-garou-kinfolk-demographics\">previous thread</a> I tried to crowdsource/poll what the ratio should be between kinfolk and Garou. I didn't get many responses as it seemed that this was something most STs and players didn't care about it. But it was one of the topics that eventually lead to this one as I worked on how to incorporate Kinfolk more into my chronicles. I use a ratio of about 100 Kinfolk to 1 Garou in terms of creating batches of Kinfolk community in my setting (there can be offsite communities as well to produce Lost Cubs and such). That isn't a strict demographic reality, just a guideline I use as ST in creating the setting. But other people might use a ratio of 30, or 250, or more. Adjust accordingly. I believe there is probably a decent chunk of Kenning Kinfolk that at any one time won't have a Garou &quot;guardian&quot;, but still embedded into the community, still loyal to the Garou, and still present. These SHOULD be doing something. Their neighbors who are providing additional &quot;taxes&quot; or &quot;tithes&quot; would grow very resentful if they don't, and I don't see the sept not wanting to make use of these resources - whether it be their finances, skills, time, and so on.<br /> <br /> But what should those expectations be? On one hand, I expect the burden of supporting the Garou should be less. On the other, the &quot;benefits&quot; of having a Garou close by is also less.<br /> <br /> Here are some current thoughts.<br /> <br /> There is still a financial contribution to the sept. This could be the equivalent of a 1% tax or other minor contribution. Perhaps the &quot;Church&quot; sends out a special basket where everyone is expected to pinch in $5 or $20 a week or whatever the amount it. Or a trusted kinfolk is entrusted to drop by the various businesses and elite families of town (without a Garou guardian) and collect a similar &quot;donation&quot; (that is voluntary, but not really voluntary because social pressure is so immense). It could be collected in various ways. Donating is a sign that the kinfolk accepts the authority of the Garou and proof they still want to be protected. Kinfolk without the means may not need to donate (the well-to-do are expected to make up for them), but they may still need to make a symbolic donation as proof of submission/obedience. The burden is not anywhere near it is for those families with a Garou directly over them, but is made up by having a much broader tax base.<br /> <br /> There is an expectation that report suspicious activity. &quot;Suspicious&quot; being outsider humans who show up to the community. They should be monitored, and their activities reported to the sept. &quot;Un-Garoulike activity&quot; needs to be reported and prevented if possible. Children playing games of the World of Shadow from Black Dog Game Factory? That's a no-no. People asking for certain books at the library (never there, but potentially available through interlibrary loan), or looking up certain websites, or other forbidden research - inform the Garou. Strange behavior by certain animals? Tell the Garou. Perhaps even other odd things like - no dogs as pets allowed (cats are OK) - that the Garou either disaprove of, or must be regulated in order to better service the caern totem. A nearby caern of justice or fertility or healing or wisdom might spill over into a kinfolk community, and the Garou want the caern to be properly supported as a result. Or mandatory attendance at &quot;festivals&quot; that are pseudo- or semi-Gaian holidays. Or as mentioned in an earlier post total silence about certain topics of conversation. It could be things like ringing a church bell if outsiders enter the town so everyone knows to be on good behavior for the Veil. These would be things applied broadly towards the whole community. It could also mean that if a person ever tries to sell property to non-kinfolk, that the Garou sept must approve. And that certain things discovered by lawyers or doctors (which would normally be protected by confidentiality) must be reported to the Garou. No letting an outsider inherit land. No abortions allowed unless the Garou sept approves. We're getting into Folk Horror territory here - something similar to the villagers in the Wicker Man or Harvest Home. These kinds of activities don't require constant action, but when the even triggers it, they're expected to obey automatically.<br /> <br /> Then there would be the VIPs in town - the village president or mayor, chief of police or firefighters, head of any businesses, heads of prominent families - these get much more oversight. They must report to the Sept Council or a trusted Kinfolk representative who reports directly to a Garou. Perhaps the wife or husband of the Sept Elder who serves as the community matriarch or patriarch. Or someone else equally trusted and respected by the Garou. These people have much more responsibilities since they are the town leaders, and the Garou must control them. For all practical purposes, they are treated like having a &quot;guardian&quot; but the burden is lessened that much of what is asked for is provided by the town in general as opposed to reaching deep into their own pockets.<br /> <br /> I won't mention mating because I think that essentially involves claiming that kinfolk, and I want to discuss later when we talk about guardianship.<br /> <br /> Is there anything I didn't mention that I should have? Anything you disagree with? Other comments?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T22:05:40-07:00","id":1398288,"title":"","content":"If these kinfolk are part of a community integrated with humans, such as Glass Walkers in the city, this kind of stuff may be a lot harder since it can't be done openly, and the number of families controlled this way diminishes. I think that is fine as part of the setting. I think Urrah kinfolk communities are very different than non-Urrah. So things need to be changed and reskinned appropriately. But in terms of the types of ways these Kinfolk are controlled, or are expected to behave, I think are similar.<br /> <br /> And of course, kinfolk in the city likely have much more of a need to be protected by local Garou. Chances of an encounter with a vampire or fomori is much higher, so wanting to keep in good stead with the local sept or other Garou authority makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T01:50:24-07:00","id":1398310,"title":"","content":"One bit on the kinfolk relation to the Garou nation - and the control level - is the utility of kinfolk to the nation. Kinfolk can hold roles that Garou can't due to the risks to the Veil. There is also the option of kinfolk as plants within human society<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">one example been that several high ranking members of SAD are kinfolk and direct investigations away from the Garou (taken from <i>Project Twighlight</i>)</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Also another factor I think that is missing in general looking through this thread is that for many (if not most) Garou some of the kinfolk they support will be one of their parents. That kinfolk are actual family, and not just a notional one. Thus they are part of the culture and not just subservient to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T04:44:57-07:00","id":1398330,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26145_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26145\" data-vbnamecard=\"26145\">babi_gog</a> love the spoiler! Didn\u2019t know that.<br /> <br /> I think in general Kinfolk are expected to choose a Garou mate and have kids with them, and they\u2019re strongly discouraged from falling in love or marrying outside the community, but they\u2019re also never forced to get involved with a particular Garou if they don\u2019t like the person that way either.<br /> <br /> Remember, forbidden love makes for some amazing plotlines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T06:25:38-07:00","id":1398343,"title":"","content":"The FBI speaking of which Had one Freeform I was in where an SAD Agent tried spying on a garou and kin on their honeymoon.... Spying with :Astral projection.<br /> <br /> Then wound up as Slave they were planning to send back loaded with BS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T07:05:06-07:00","id":1398349,"title":"","content":"Spying on a couple on their honeymoon is REALLY messed up. Even for SAD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T08:39:23-07:00","id":1398367,"title":"","content":"Does sending them back loaded with BS sound like a reasonable thing to do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T08:40:00-07:00","id":1398368,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> I am very impressed with how much thought you've put into this topic. After rereading W20, again, I have realized just how important Kinfolk are, not just for Garou but all Fera, due to the Curse, and just how illogical some of the Fera PC templates are, with these roles much better filled by Kinfolk.<br /> <br /> This has been very thought provoking foe me and will definitely have an impact in future games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T09:58:34-07:00","id":1398375,"title":"","content":"I remember when 5th edition got announced, a website went up, and the werewolf tribes had sections talking about what kind of day jobs they had... <br /> *shudders*<br /> <br /> But, I don't actually think kinfolk are fundamentally neccessary for garou beyond breeding and in land ownership in areas where that may be an issue. Garou don't need money, they can hunt for food, they can be entirely self sufficient without relying on kin. It's only in areas where a caern can be purchased that kinfolk have more value, or with tribes that value a connection with humanity. Even if you enjoy kinfolk working jobs and acquiring money, most garou are still aware that they can drop all that if they wanted to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T14:23:54-07:00","id":1398436,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> and thanks from me too. After reading this thread I\u2019m defo gonna pick up A Breed Apart. Kinfolk are really important to a Garou and if I ever do play a Werewolf character I want to make sure she (or he) has a strong family structure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T18:13:06-07:00","id":1398480,"title":"","content":"There have always been weird templates and characters in the Rage Across and Tribe/Fera books because of the Curse. I remember several threads on this forum over the years about them. If you take the Curse seriously, many of these characters just aren't viable or realistic unless you assume they ONLY interact with Kinfolk. They couldn't do their jobs among ordinary humans. And even among Kinfolk, it can be questionable.<br /> <br /> But certainly some Garou can work among humans. Ragabash who don't raise their Rage could do so, and I expect many Ragabash function as infiltrators among the Flock. Theurges could likely do so as well except that for many, their duties in the Umbra would conflict. Philodox are likely the last auspice who could hold most jobs as well although they'd need to avoid a substantial amount of humanity. Galliards and Ahrouns just have too much Rage. But I could see them holding certain jobs and following certain circumstances (thug in a criminal gang, any job where they work at home or do it alone, a place where they only meet Kinfolk). But even here, the threat of Frenzy should see them removed as any Rage roll could result in Frenzy for them (so even holding jobs among Kinfolk may not be smart). I think in the past when 90% of humanity were peasant farmers and Garou could live with their kinfolk family on some homestead or work as hunters of woodsmen, that holding a job was easier.<br /> <br /> I also think that for many Garou, a typical 9-5 job would simply get in the way of their auspice duties and responsibilities to their pack and sept. 40+ hours a week eats up a lot of time that could be spent investigating Wyrm taint, building relationships with spirits, learning and practicing rites, patrolling the caern, studying the Litany, Silver Record, or other Garou lore, and planning attacks on Wyrm minions. I can see <i>some</i> Garou concentrating on interacting with the Flock. There are appropriate character and pack concepts that would do so. But I don't think most Garou would do so. They would want to limit that and keep it as flexible as possible so it doesn't inconvenience them for more important things only they can do.<br /> <br /> Creating a character by focusing on an occupation is an easy to distinguish one character from another, so I'm not surprised many writers and STs do that. But it is actually a bad approach for Garou because it ignores the limitations of the Curse. Their backgrounds would need to include more information in order to justify it.<br /> <br /> I also believe many people place Garou directly into the world of the Flock (where these issues are more important) rather than explicitly limiting them to a Kinfolk only community.<br /> <br /> In games that I've played (and run), Kinfolk has always been a secondary characteristic of the setting. Something acknowledged as being in the background or part of a character's Backgrounds or backstory, but that's it. Not something prominent in the setting. Lately, I've been trying to fix it and make Kinfolk much more prominent because I think it is a positive for the setting. So it is good to hear others are doing so as well because of this thread.<br /> <br /> A large part of this is reading and watching some classics of Folk Horror like Wicker Man and Harvest Home. I thought they were ideal examples for kinfolk communities, and I wanted to do something like that for my setting. So I started planting various settlements of kinfolks here and there. Differentiating them - not just be tribal affiliation, but their exclusivity or integration with the Flock, their attitudes to Garou and human society and values, and what Garou if any are part of it. And creating institutions like a boarding school, a private sanitarium, private banks, law firms with exclusive clients, and fraternal socities that are entirely kinfolk and used by the Garou. As a result, it's raised some questions in how I should interact with PCs once they make contact with these people, and thinking how I can enrich my PCs roleplay.<br /> <br /> So thanks for any compliments. If I've given any thought to this, it's because I've been struggling as to the practical application of this. So I'm using this thread as a sounding board to determine if my ideas sound right before I start exposing them to my players. I'd rather this group comment first and save me from potential conflicts with my players if I get something wrong. So the comments here do help me - letting me know I'm on the right track, and sparking new ideas as people make their own contributions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T18:18:55-07:00","id":1398486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1398375#post1398375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember when 5th edition got announced, a website went up, and the werewolf tribes had sections talking about what kind of day jobs they had...<br /> *shudders*<br /> <br /> But, I don't actually think kinfolk are fundamentally neccessary for garou beyond breeding and in land ownership in areas where that may be an issue. Garou don't need money, they can hunt for food, they can be entirely self sufficient without relying on kin. It's only in areas where a caern can be purchased that kinfolk have more value, or with tribes that value a connection with humanity. Even if you enjoy kinfolk working jobs and acquiring money, most garou are still aware that they can drop all that if they wanted to.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is actually not true. Most garou, no matter how much they yap about humanity being bad, WANT and NEED human contact. Maybe some Elders could, but most garou still want their cars, jeans, clothes, playing cards and such. That is the whole issue with Red Talons, most garou are too human to get their point. In lots of books, they are called outright psychopaths by other garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T18:22:54-07:00","id":1398489,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar110_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"110\" data-vbnamecard=\"110\">Ana Mizuki</a> exactly. You said what I was thinking very eloquently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T23:59:20-07:00","id":1398536,"title":"","content":"Something to add to level of overall sept control over general Kinfolk population: it is probably the Sept Council that makes decisions like they feel it would be very useful to have someone work in the phone company as an installer of equipment, or that they want someone to enter law practice and eventually become a judge, or that they want someone to attempt to join the FBI, or some other big career decision in order to help out the sept. An individual Garou could do that as well, but an individual attempting to do so is likely trying to build a power base. The Sept Council is more likely to do so for a genuine need and their decision offers a legitimacy to it.<br /> <br /> It may be something that originates within the sept itself, or is discussed at some concolation, and the septs who attended try to implement that on the local level.<br /> <br /> I don't think the sept picks some kinfolk and tells them what to do specifically. Instead, I think the sept may call for volunteers among the kinfolk population. These kinds of worthwhile positions often require special training, long term commitment, and are highly competitive. Not just any kinfolk can do it. So they call for volunteers and offer compensation for succeeding. So the kinfolk who have the right talents and disposition are encouraged to select themselves and go about it. Perhaps supported by any necessary local &quot;scholarships&quot; or other support so it can be provided. In doing so, such kinfolk likely get a Garou &quot;patron&quot; or &quot;control&quot; that ends up being a guardian. So we'll talk more about that later.<br /> <br /> They may also gain other benefits and privileges like claiming mates as if they were Garou, being awarded actual Renown if they achieve that goal, and being groomed for additional leadership among the Kinfolk with Garou support. (&quot;We're going to make Bob the next mayor because he proved so useful as a lawyer these past ten years. Let everyone know he's supposed to win with 55-60% of the vote next election.&quot;)<br /> <br /> But what if they don't get volunteers? Or the people who try fail? I think the Sept Council will re-evaluate. Maybe they give up for a while, knowing they can't force these things. But sometimes the need may be so great, they do start putting immense pressure on people they think could do, but aren't stepping up to the plate. I think these social pressures can be intense. And the Garou also have Gifts that can help &quot;convince&quot; people. If the need is &quot;local&quot;, they may pass word to allied/friendly septs that they need some Kinfolk with X skill or talent, and offer an incentive for kinfolk to move to town to help out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T02:37:00-07:00","id":1398743,"title":"","content":"Odd thought : Kinfolk looking out for eachother and getting eachother into important possitions in society (not to mention garou mysteriously removing wyrmish rivals) creates reactionary conspiracy theories of secret ruling classes akin to stonemasons or &quot;the jews&quot; or lizard people, whilst left wing onlookers see nepotism and ruling bloodlines. These sentiments arent universal and it isn't always obvious, but there tends to be pushback against kinfolk sproradically, especially when someone fans the flames. Often creating an 'us vs them' environment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T16:32:02-07:00","id":1398893,"title":"","content":"Kinfolk are certainly part of a conspiracy - to keep the existence of Garou a secret and to aid them when necessary.<br /> <br /> However, what separates them from those kind of conspiracy theories is their comparative lack of power to other conspiracies that do have that influence! That would include vampires and their servants, the Technocracy, and various Wyrm minions like PENTEX, the Seventh Generation, and others. The Kinfolk simply do not control that amount of resources and influence. They likely have less collective influence than graduates of the top tier of the Ivy League.<br /> <br /> But down at the local level, there probably is a perception in some places that there is a hidden network people find it hard to place. That may happen at some Kinfolk/Garou owned or converged businesses, local government in rural, low population counties, and other institutions that are open but have a significant Kinfolk presence and they have an agenda (say within the FBI or CDC - organizations they can never control, but which are too important not to have spies in).<br /> <br /> I've compared Kinfolk before to the feel of Folk Horror stories. Certainly from the perspective of a mundane human encountering a Kinfolk community, their introduction to that community and their slowly learning of hidden secrets being kept is a well established trope in horror literature.<br /> <br /> I think that can lead to interesting setting and good stories. Kinfolk want to eliminate those kind of dangers before the Garou intervene because once the Garou intervene, there are going to be corpses. So Kinfolk will either try to make that mundane human an ally and win them over, or remove/expel them from the community before they learn too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T19:58:28-07:00","id":1398933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1397334#post1397334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anywhere that kinfolk or Garou are concentrated is a target, but a boarding school or something similar has advantages. One thing is that it is respectable. The FBI aren\u2019t going to raid a boarding school, or if they do it\u2019s going to require a lot more use of political clout to get them to do it. A boarding school can have security and in fact is a good central location that can be guarded by Garou or spirits. If the boarding school gets attacked, the attackers will be investigated by the police, not the boarding school itself. The staff can keep a close eye on the kid\u2019s to notice a first change and minimize the associated risks.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s likely safer than an off the grid compound, maybe even more secret than one too. It\u2019s also probably safer than just letting kinfolk kids live integrated with normal human kids.<br /> <br /> I can see it now - Professor Albrecht\u2019s School for Gifted Youngsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, that would be absolutely AWESOME!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T01:57:11-07:00","id":1398977,"title":"","content":"It's a bit like this novel, that didn't breed the intended series, with &quot;That Proganitor's Military Academy for Gene-Manipulated Were-Youngsters, Because Crossover&quot; - Call to battle.<br /> <br /> In our LARP world, we actually established a Silver Fang Boarding School that is magically protected and has a fairly high ranking garou staff, because it doubles as the seat of the Gleaming Eye's inquisitor.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> On the Kinfolk/Garou topic there are a lot of things written here, that I agree with. In general I'd like to point out, that before W20 Kinfolk (which I only quickly browsed through) there was the Player's Guide to Garou with the only out-of-character description about Kinfolk life. It was about a child of gaia, but anyway, it always is my reference point when discussing Kinfolk/Garou relationships and power hierarchy.<br /> <br /> &quot;Unsung Heroes&quot; is a bit critical, a some multi-page discussions here in the forums a while back show. For, the story part is mentioning a girl that sees her little brothers first change and is struck by the need to protect something as magnificent as a werewolf crinos form. And I can totally see that, plus it's her little brother. But the back of the book, with the Kinfolk of note, describes victims of garou society or single garou and delivers one, far to memorable, counter-point that doesn't do justice to majority of kinfolk-garou-relationships.<br /> <br /> And, while I can see, that exploitation and rape happen in real life and are part of the WoD, where dark plot points are part of an more mature approach to role-playing, I find it difficult to generalise garou in an abusive position over kinfolk. Especially since the source material describes this, and counterpoints, bit all to often, these counterpoints are ignored. Like &quot;Unsung Heroes&quot; goes into detail how garou tend to belittle kinfolk, as a means to protect and shield them from the dangers of the world around them. And mentions, when kinfolk come to listen to the latest exploits of the garou and cheer for them, when the tales are told in the moot and renown is ritually awarded/fixed.<br /> <br /> And, I think the already mentioned part, that is most relevant is, that the Kinfolk are the direct families of the garou, or sometimes extended families, but still, cousins and confidants, not servants, although in a Silver Fang or Shadow Lords sept, servant might be the job they have.<br /> <br /> With W20 this might have changed. W20 tells us garou aren't discernable from kinfolk until the first change (breaking with revised rulings). And since this isn't a new development, but a retcon, it in my eyes changes the whole dynamic, because, you can't bully or mistreat a kinfolk any more, without the risk that next summer said kinfolk will have a fist change, and be a revengeful opponent fostern the summer after that. With the whole possibility that any kinfolk could change at any time, the whole background of Samuel Haight makes so much less sense.<br /> Also, did I retroactively breach the litany, if the other parent of my child has a first change later? I really thing W20 dropped the ball here.<br /> <br /> From the elements of W20 Kinfolk that I saw I wasn't amazed either. Gifts and Rites to Kinfolk sure seem to make them more accessible as PCs but still, a garou/kin-combned troupe doesn't make too much sense, especially since garou should make an effort to go into harms way, but leave the kinfolk apart from danger as good as possible. I can see, how it can make sense to have a werewolf game where all Players have a secondary kinfolk character (possibly tied to another PC), so that the parts of stories or scenes that garou normally wouldn't engage in (especially due to the Curse) can be played, too.<br /> But, the game is werewolf, for the most part, and should be played by werewolves. If one runs a kinfolk game, the whole dynamic is different and it can be it's own worthwhile game, but one decides to go that route, one doesn't need Gifts/Rites for that isn't, in my opinion, fitting the moot of the game.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> Regarding rape as a game element. Well, it is a difficult matter and it is hard to know how to incorporate as an element into the game.<br /> A while back, there was a plot in the TV show &quot;Switched at Birth&quot;, where drunken sex happened. And for the woman this was a shameful, drunken mistake until another woman heard the story and named the incident rape. Based on the fact, that the male in the relationship should have known that the woman was too drunk to remember in the morning what lead to the sex. And while no criminal charges become part of the story in the TV show, there is a loss of scholarship and associating the male's name to rape because of google.<br /> And I think this shows to some extend, how broadly the perception of what rape is can vary. That is, if there isn't consent, it is rape - sure. But if the consent is due to bilateral intoxication, well, I wouldn't want to be a judge or college disciplinary board member to rule on that.<br /> <br /> And with garou/kinfolk communities and their possibly jaded or non-normal views towards duties and role-models I can totally see Albrechts Mother to feel like another child was her duty, or garou and kin to have intercourse because some rite named them a good match, or because she was the maiden of the spring festival and he won all the festivals challenges - and so on. If consent springs from an education that is not what we perceive as normal, it is still consent, or isn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T02:16:57-07:00","id":1398982,"title":"","content":"Sorry, wrong thread<br /> <br /> Edit; I agree. Being able to tell which kinfolk would change or not (with some room for error) is more interesting and makes more sense than being completely blind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 06-26-2020, 05:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T03:12:52-07:00","id":1398992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1398982#post1398982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit; I agree. Being able to tell which kinfolk would change or not (with some room for error) is more interesting and makes more sense than being completely blind.</div> </div> </div> </div>The margin of error was the imminent flaw of the &quot;Scent of the true form&quot; gift pre-W20. Two simple sentences like &quot;Although the gift works automatic on detecting garou, it is known to be flawed occasionally when used on pre-First Change garou children. So, some kids aren't detected as garou and don't receive the Baptism of Fire, but most are.&quot; would have left enough room for Lost Cubs, but still allow for all the other background stories.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T15:58:47-07:00","id":1399154,"title":"","content":"I've been away from my computer a lot this week because of irl stuff but coming back to it (and these forums) I do have to say that I am fascinated by a lot of the stuff you've been suggesting Black Fox and I do feel that 'Folk Horror' is a very good term to describe a great deal of the Garou Nation with perhaps the Glass Walkers &amp; Red Talons being the few exceptions and more then making up for it with their own Techno-Horror and Primal Horror elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T16:38:14-07:00","id":1400205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1398992#post1398992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The margin of error was the imminent flaw of the &quot;Scent of the true form&quot; gift pre-W20. Two simple sentences like &quot;Although the gift works automatic on detecting garou, it is known to be flawed occasionally when used on pre-First Change garou children. So, some kids aren't detected as garou and don't receive the Baptism of Fire, but most are.&quot; would have left enough room for Lost Cubs, but still allow for all the other background stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer this kind of style too, and it's one of the house rule changes to W20 I made. The way I run it is if you fail, you don't detect pre-change Garou as Garou. You think they are kinfolk. Or you think a kinfolk is a pre-Change Garou. If you botch it, somehow it fails that for everyone until at some point post-puberty it resets. There's not necessarily a cause-and-effect relationship there. I just want to avoid &quot;shotgunning&quot; situations where people could theoretically keep testing until they get it right. The &quot;botch&quot; simply means something has gone wrong. And there are simply anomalous cases (ST fiat) where it's never going to work. Or that the difficulty to detect is higher than normal.<br /> <br /> I want detection to work most of the time, but not that it is infallible.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T16:59:58-07:00","id":1400207,"title":"","content":"So the next point I'd like to discuss is the idea of Garou &quot;guardians&quot; being appointed over kinfolk. Previous posters have posted something like this, and I've seen this used in various online games. I think there are different terms that can be used, but I think the concept is more or less the same.<br /> <br /> I think this is an important issue for a couple of reasons.<br /> <br /> First, this is essentially an issue of a Garou claiming control over kinfolk. So this is something most Garou will do in order to get a mate. Or perhaps adopt kinfolk into their family. It can also be used for less noble reasons like really wanting to control the financial resources of a kinfolk owned business or other feudal or exploitative scenario about controlling resources.<br /> <br /> Second, this involves potential conflict with other Garou. Either because it means moving onto another Garou's territory (I want to marry a sister of that other Garou; she wants to, but the Garou doesn't. So there are rival claims. Let's challenge it out.), or because two or more Garou want the same kinfolk (for mating, to access the family fortune, etc.) So there is good conflict here for STs.<br /> <br /> Third, it also involves a general claim against the sept in general which is already providing some measure of indirect (or direct) control over that &quot;asset.&quot; What is the Sept Council doesn't see that individual Garou as being trustworthy to control someone that vital to the sept? They think the Garou may botch it up. Or they are &quot;holding&quot; that kinfolk for some other Garou to return or come of age, or whatever. In other words, there may be greater issues involved for that <i>particular </i>kinfolk that the sept leadership would intervene when they wouldn't for the majority of kinfolk.<br /> <br /> Fourth, there may be instances a Garou doesn't want to be responsible for that kinfolk, but the sept or tribe assigns them anyway. Maybe the kinfolk is a troublemaker, a screw up, or has some sordid past. The sept or tribe has decided somehow needs to look out for that kinfolk (either temporarily or permanently), and someone needs to get stuck with the job.<br /> <br /> Fifth, there is the issue that maybe it is the kinfolk who is appealing for a guardian, and how does the sept or other Garou react to that? Maybe someone knows that a Garou will claim them as a mate, and they don't want that so they try to get another Garou involved in their lives pre-emptively. Or maybe they hope it'll lead to romantic affection down the line. Or they just really like that Garou and trust that Garou to do what is right for them. Or fear their business may one day come under attack of a vampire rival or other supernatural enemy, and they want an ally who can defend them.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there are other issues involved in this scenario that I'm just not thinking of. So feel free to add more buckets or considerations.<br /> <br /> So I think there's lots of potential here for STs to use in their chronicles. And all of this involves Garou law and Kinfolk rights. So we need to determine a set of general principles and general rights in order to figure out how they apply to any one situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T23:36:02-07:00","id":1400647,"title":"","content":"I can see that some septs, with high numbers of associated kinfolk, would appoint a garou or pack as point of contact and possibly also task him with the overall well-being and concern for the kinfolk community. Also, in cases where a sept reforms itself after a mass-casualties battle or years of neglect there might be a need for the garou to task some pack with locating and re-integrating kinfolk into the sept structures.<br /> Since kinfolk start out as the families and relatives of a sept's garou there might be some effort needed it these garou have fallen and therefore the kinfolk family lost connection with the rest of the sept. That is, if the kinfolf families weren't intertwined to begin with.<br /> <br /> Regarding the first scenario: I don't see most septs, depending on tribe, would allow a garou to stand up before the community and proclaim &quot;this kinfolk is mine, and I control him/her like my property&quot;. While proclamations of protection, and/or integration into the extended family and of course marriage-like pairings are imo more in tune with how garou handle such matters. And, I'd assume, such proclamations are consented to by the kinfolk, if an adult.<br /> That doesn't mean that a garou can't believe and try to force that in such cases the kinfolk are then theirs to control, but kinfolk communities and other garou might object to such behaviour and mindsets.<br /> <br /> About the second scenario: &quot;Well, see, this garou I don't know and have no family relationship with wants proclaims that I am now his to be controlled. All he wants is my family fortune, that my ancestors, garou and kin alike, and myself have build with hard work and protected with cunning, wisdom and compassion against the minions of the wyrm. I'm not a garou, I am beneath you, but how is making such unfounded claims showing respect for me and my relatives, living and dead. We are all of Gaia, aren't we?&quot;<br /> Hey, who wouldn't be flattered, if two young athletic girls would sink teeth and claws into each other, preferably in a mud wrestling contest, just to determine who I'm allowed to fuck later. And while I some garou see their partners as their property, I think number of garou who do so is not that much higher as the ratio amongst humans who see their partners in that way.<br /> <br /> I totally get scenario three. Garou and senior kinfolk alike have hopes and dreams and plans on how who their sons/daughters marry and how their septs should look like and who deserves what - and they may take action (or deny action of others) to shape their septs that way.<br /> <br /> Scenario four sounds like a garou and a kinfolk SC need a reason to stick together, so the NPCs make them. But sure, someone has to keep an eye out for a troublemaker and if you do not have senior kinfolk members to do so, a young garou might be the influencer you need to assign to the job.<br /> <br /> I also get scenario five. I totally can see that kinfolk would want to involve themselves with certain garou for reasons they believe to be beneficial for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T02:14:30-07:00","id":1401304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1400647#post1400647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the first scenario: I don't see most septs, depending on tribe, would allow a garou to stand up before the community and proclaim &quot;this kinfolk is mine, and I control him/her like my property&quot;. While proclamations of protection, and/or integration into the extended family and of course marriage-like pairings are imo more in tune with how garou handle such matters. And, I'd assume, such proclamations are consented to by the kinfolk, if an adult.<br /> That doesn't mean that a garou can't believe and try to force that in such cases the kinfolk are then theirs to control, but kinfolk communities and other garou might object to such behaviour and mindsets.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm looking for a &quot;standard&quot; with the understanding that some tribes and septs will deviate from it.<br /> <br /> My view of Garou society is that they are, for the most part, an extremely traditional people. So while things like arranged marriages are no longer the norm in Western countries, they were the norm historically there and are still the norm in many non-Western societies. So many rural septs and attached kinfolk settlements are still like that at least with kenning kinfolk. More integrated communities are much less so.<br /> <br /> And using that as the basis means Garou can often claim things without &quot;consent&quot; because the culture of those communities still acknowledge such authority as legitimate. Other kinfolk communities wouldn't acknowledge it as legitimate, and with those it can't be done. Some communities are in a period of transition, and they still happen but provoke conflict.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1400647#post1400647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the second scenario: &quot;Well, see, this garou I don't know and have no family relationship with wants proclaims that I am now his to be controlled. All he wants is my family fortune, that my ancestors, garou and kin alike, and myself have build with hard work and protected with cunning, wisdom and compassion against the minions of the wyrm. I'm not a garou, I am beneath you, but how is making such unfounded claims showing respect for me and my relatives, living and dead. We are all of Gaia, aren't we?&quot;<br /> Hey, who wouldn't be flattered, if two young athletic girls would sink teeth and claws into each other, preferably in a mud wrestling contest, just to determine who I'm allowed to fuck later. And while I some garou see their partners as their property, I think number of garou who do so is not that much higher as the ratio amongst humans who see their partners in that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I think this is something that has a wide range depending on tribes and septs. It's important to determine in what cultures such Garou claims and controls have legitimacy among the kinfolk. And I think besides the kind of claims that can be made, there is also the issue of what limits exist to those claims and what absolute rights kinfolk have. I made an earlier post on this thread about how many resources can be taken in this way, and what has to be left alone. There is also the issue of how much wealth and power is seen as residing in the individual versus community claims. As such, I think when speaking of Garou culture, while it is legitimate for a kinfolk to talk about &quot;unfounded claims&quot; and &quot;respect&quot; and such. I also think the Garou claimant can make counter arguments using the Litany.<br /> <br /> And many of these claims may need to be couched in certain terms in order to get legitimacy to them. For example, in order to assuage the concerns of a kinfolk that a Garou may be claiming them in order to get a hold of resources that kinfolk wants to reserve for his family, I potentially see something like the sept agreeing with the kinfolk in general, but since he has an unmarried daughter, that they've decided the best solution is for that Garou to marry/mate with that daughter so that the kinfolk's concerns and the Garou's claims are met. That may not be the intended outcome of the kinfolk, but I can see it as a potential &quot;solution&quot; the sept leadership provides. Not necessarily so. But it is an option.<br /> <br /> I think kinfolk occupy a special place. In one sense, I do think the Garou see them as livestock and pets. They're economic resources and beloved companions, but not &quot;people&quot;. But in another sense, human kinfolk are obviously not animals and therefore enjoy certain rights. But I don't think kinfolk are &quot;equal&quot; to Garou in terms of Garou law, and Garou see themselves above them in the same sense adults are above children in human society. This thread is to help me and others figure out what sweet spot they want for their chronicles. I don't think everyone will come to the same decision, but I do hope this thread can help them figure that out. So thanks for making these points. I think they help everyone clarify things in their own heads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  fixed some typos 07-07-2020, 04:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T12:39:15-07:00","id":1401538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1401304#post1401304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm looking for a &quot;standard&quot; with the understanding that some tribes and septs will deviate from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course.<br /> My statement meant to convey, that I don't see this scenario within the &quot;standard&quot;, deviations from septs of certain tribes not withstanding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1401304#post1401304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My view of Garou society is that they are, for the most part, an extremely traditional people. So while things like arranged marriages are no longer the norm in Western countries, they were the norm historically there and are still the norm in many non-Western societies. So many rural septs and attached kinfolk settlements are still like that at least with kenning kinfolk. More integrated communities are much less so.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. And I see that families, kin and garou alike, make these arranged marriages and force them on the next generation. Meaning the adult generation, force their decisions on the adolescent generation by instilling a sense of duty in them or call it romantic, or plain force them.<br /> And most likely garou have a higher standing within the family as a whole and therefore more say in the matter. Also they can argue with signs/vision, granted by the spirits, and political implications the kinfolk family elders aren't aware of, but in the end, for the most part, the family &quot;elder&quot; make make the decision and enforce it.<br /> I mean, these arranged marriages are for garou, too.<br /> &quot;Yes, boy, you are my second son, but you are born garou, and you have to marry the the eldest age-appropriate daughter of the Riversinde sept's Jarl, because that is the deal we made. I might just be kin, but your grandfather, may his spirit dwell in the homeland happily, made that deal and you have to respect your Elder, even if he's dead now. So, suck it up.&quot;<br /> <br /> And sure, if a family doesn't have any true born garou with appropriate standing, the kin-family matriarch can petition the sept Elder to back an arranged marriage for her true born granddaughter, because of politics. <br /> <br /> In any case, I see that one generation forces their decisions on the next, and possibly on members of their own generation, if there are unwed or widowed siblings. But I don't see garou claiming kinfolk as property. Someone calling out that a marriage was arranged and agreed upon and therefore the kin has to deliver, sure. But making a claim, without any pre-existing circumstances, like an arranged marriage, I would find untypical for garou. For kinfolk, just like anything else, aren't just up for grabs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1401304#post1401304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And using that as the basis means Garou can often claim things without &quot;consent&quot; because the culture of those communities still acknowledge such authority as legitimate. Other kinfolk communities wouldn't acknowledge it as legitimate, and with those it can't be done. Some communities are in a period of transition, and they still happen but provoke conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, my thoughts above not withstanding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1401304#post1401304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I think this is something that has a wide range depending on tribes and septs. It's important to determine in what cultures such Garou claims and controls have legitimacy among the kinfolk. And I think besides the kind of claims that can be made, there is also the issue of what limits exist to those claims and what absolute rights kinfolk have. I made an earlier post on this thread about how many resources can be taken in this way, and what has to be left alone. There is also the issue of how much wealth and power is seen as residing in the individual versus community claims. As such, I think when speaking of Garou culture, while it is legitimate for a kinfolk to talk about &quot;unfounded claims&quot; and &quot;respect&quot; and such. I also think the Garou claimant can make counter arguments using the Litany.</div> </div> </div> </div>By what tenant of the Litany?<br /> - My wealth, as kinfolk family head, is not a share of the kill, it is my territory, however.<br /> - I might be, right now childless and unmarried, but my wealth should be the resources of my future true born child or grandchild.<br /> - My riches are the spoils of my labour, and if I decide that I spend it, that is my right. You might want that I bribe the county clerk to declare your packs hunting grounds a natural protection site, but the 'Sweet water' Packs hunting grounds are right next to my farm and their hunting grounds would profit from such bribery just the same.<br /> <br /> I think that any claim for mastery over an adult kinfolk, and basically robbing that person of their rights, would need to have a foundation that makes sense. Having dominion over an under-aged kinfolk, or some kinfolk who's reckless or undisclosed actions posed a threat to the sept in the past, or something like that, yes, that makes sense. But without that the claim is without honour and for the sept to allow it would be unwise.<br /> <br /> That's not withstanding any tradition to, for example, include a widow(er) or otherwise single-kinfolk person into the own family, taking a position with rights and obligations normal for kinfolk families in that sept/tribes culture.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1401304#post1401304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And many of these claims may need to be couched in certain terms in order to get legitimacy to them. For example, in order to assuage the concerns of a kinfolk that a Garou may be claiming them in order to get a hold of resources that kinfolk wants to reserve for his family, I potentially see something like the sept agreeing with the kinfolk in general, but since he has an unmarried daughter, that they've decided the best solution is for that Garou to marry/mate with that daughter so that the kinfolk's concerns and the Garou's claims are met. That may not be the intended outcome of the kinfolk, but I can see it as a potential &quot;solution&quot; the sept leadership provides. Not necessarily so. But it is an option.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. That is a scenario that I find makes sense in garou society.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395242-garou-control-over-kinfolk-a-discussion-warning-triggering-subject-matter?p=1401304#post1401304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think kinfolk occupy a special place. In one sense, I do think the Garou see them as livestock and pets. They're economic resources and beloved companions, but not &quot;people&quot;. But in another sense, human kinfolk are obviously not animals and therefore enjoy certain rights. But I don't think kinfolk are &quot;equal&quot; to Garou in terms of Garou law, and Garou see themselves above them in the same sense adults are above children in human society. This thread is to help me and others figure out what sweet spot they want for their chronicles. I don't think everyone will come to the same decision, but I do hope this thread can help them figure that out. So thanks for making these points. I think they help everyone clarify things in their own heads.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that garou see them above kinfolk as adults see them above children. It also is what 'Kinfolk: Unsung Heros' has as it's default relationship. And, as a lost cub, you obviously don't have personal relationships to the sept's kinfolk to begin with. They aren't the parents who taught you and raised you, growing up. They aren't the siblings and childhood friends who were the centre of your daily life until the first change. They are just groupies, who pay for the sept's holdings and do all the stuff that is boring, while you are the gaia-chosen warrior saving the world.<br /> That is, if the sept doesn't have a Nana (a kinfolk Den Parent) - which according to W20 Kinfolk doesn't exist - and said Nana brought you up to speed on all things garou before you were send on your Rite of Passage.<br /> But for all the other garou, that are born garou raised by kenning kinfolk or (as of W20) were kenning kinfolk themselves before they had their first change? It's hard to argue that they see their direct relatives as pets and livestock.<br /> &quot;The Millers, down the street, sure, they are just there to make fun of and take whatever they have if you want - not because they are kinfolk, but because they are Bone Gnawer kin....&quot;<br /> <br /> With the garou septs and the kenning kinkolk living interwoven life there are a lot of personal relationships and with the kinfolk usually having the majority of the young non-lost-cub upbringing as time to make an impression, I find such a mindset, strange. Even in medieval times, with more lupus garou in the mix, adding their world-view on kinfolk to sept's baseline, I wouldn't get a &quot;livestock and pets&quot; as a sept's common routine. That a single garou leader, especially a follower of Grandfather Thunder, would adopt this point of view, sure, but such a person has a totally different baseline on what power means, who minions are (everyone) and what one is entitled to (everything).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}